hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"601","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Sabbah al-Shami narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz al-Shami, from his father, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Abu Ayyub, shall I not point you to a charity with whose place Allah and His Messenger will be pleased? He said: Yes indeed. He said: You make peace between people when they are corrupt with one another, and bring them close when they are distant."
"602","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam Abu Imran al-Tujibi, the freedman of Tujib, who said: We were at Constantinople, with Fadalalah ibn Ubayd al-Ansari over the people of Syria and Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani over the people of Egypt. A great line of Romans came out to us, and a great line of Muslims went out, and a Muslim man charged the Roman line and killed among them, then came back. The people shouted and said: Glory be to Allah, he has cast himself into destruction with his own hands. Then Abu Ayyub al-Ansari stood and said: O people, you interpret this verse upon other than its interpretation. This verse was revealed concerning us, the company of the Ansar: when Allah Almighty strengthened His religion and multiplied its supporters, we said secretly among ourselves, apart from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Our wealth has been neglected, so if we stayed with it and repaired what has been neglected of it - then Allah Almighty revealed this verse, answering what we had resolved in ourselves, that we stay with our wealth and repair what has been neglected of it. The destruction was what we had intended to do, and we were commanded to wage war. Abu Ayyub never ceased waging war until Allah Almighty took him."
"603","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, he said: A man who heard Abu Ayyub narrated to me that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray the sunset prayer at the breaking of the fast of the fasting person, hastening before the rising of the stars."
"604","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, having heard Abu al-Bakhtari narrating from Abu Said, who said: When this chapter was revealed, When the help of Allah comes and the victory, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it until he completed it, then said: I and my companions are one party, and the people are another party; there is no emigration after the conquest. Abu Said said: I narrated this hadith to Marwan ibn al-Hakam - who was governor of Medina - and he said: You have lied, while Zayd ibn Thabit and Zayd ibn Arqam were with him. I said: These two, had they wished, would have narrated to you; but this one fears you may strip him of the charity office, and this one fears you may strip him of the leadership of his people. He raised the stick at me, and when they saw that, they said: He has spoken the truth."
"605","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, the orators of the Ansar stood, and some of them said: O company of Emigrants, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man from among you he would join a man from among us with him; so we think this matter should be held by two men, a man from among you and a man from among us. Then Zayd ibn Thabit stood and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was from among the Emigrants, and we were the helpers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the leader shall only be from among the Emigrants, and we are his helpers just as we were the helpers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, said: May Allah reward you, O company of the Ansar, with good from among a tribe, and may He confirm your speaker. By Allah, had you said other than this we would not have reconciled with you."
"606","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: We ate the pre-dawn meal with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we went out to the prayer."
"607","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked toward Yemen and said: O Allah, turn their hearts toward us. Then he looked toward Syria and said: O Allah, turn their hearts toward us. Then he looked toward Iraq and said: O Allah, turn their hearts toward us, and bless for us our sa and our mudd."
"608","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father Thabit, who said: I walked with Anas, and he began taking short steps. He said: O Thabit, why do you not ask me why I do this with you? I said: And why do you do it? He said: I walked with Zayd ibn Thabit, and he did the same with me, and said: Why do you not ask me why I do this with you? So I asked him, and Zayd said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did the same with me, and said to me: O Zayd, do you know why I do this with you? I said: And why did you do it? He said: I wanted our steps to the mosque to be many."
"609","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Ansari narrating from Zayd ibn Thabit, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Uhud, a group of those with him turned back. The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) split into two parties concerning them: one party saying, we kill them, and one party saying, no. Then this verse was revealed: What is the matter with you that you are two parties concerning the hypocrites, while Allah has cast them back for what they earned - the whole verse."
"610","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Ansari narrating from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is Taybah (Medina), and it expels its filth just as fire expels the dross of silver."
"611","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq informed me that Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to him, saying: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, sent for me at the time of the killing of the people of Yamamah, and Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, was with him. He said: This one came to me and informed me that the killing has fallen heavily upon the reciters of the Quran - meaning on the day of Yamamah - and I fear the killing may fall heavily upon the reciters of the Quran in the other battlefields, so the Quran will go. I have decided that you collect it. I said: How do you do something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? By Allah, had they burdened me with moving a mountain from among the mountains, it would have been dearer to me than what they burdened me with."
"612","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Kharijah ibn Zayd informed me, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I missed a verse which I used to hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite, so I sought it and found it with Khuzaymah ibn Thabit: Among the believers are men who were true to what they pledged to Allah - so I attached it in its chapter."
"613","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This wealth is green and sweet, so sell not the fruits until their ripeness appears."
"614","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri: Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq narrated to us that Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to him, saying: I lost a verse which I used to hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite, so I sought it and found it with Khuzaymah ibn Thabit: There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves - the verse - so I attached it in its chapter."
"615","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from al-Qasim ibn Hassan, who said: Wadiat al-Ansari sent me to Zayd ibn Thabit to ask him about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in fear. I came to him and asked him, and he narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with his Companions and divided them: one group facing their enemy, and one group facing him. He prayed one rakah with those near him, then they went to the ranks of their brothers, then the others came and he prayed one rakah with them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two rakahs, and the people had one rakah each."
"616","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I recited al-Najm before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not prostrate in it."
"617","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: I heard Yunus ibn Jubayr narrating from Kathir ibn al-Salt, that they were writing the codices with Zayd ibn Thabit, and they came upon this verse. Zayd ibn Thabit said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The old man and the old woman, when they commit adultery, stone them outright, as a deterrent from Allah and His Messenger."
"618","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Sulayman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aban, from his father, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Thabit saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Three things the heart of a Muslim harbors no treachery against: sincerity of deed for Allah Almighty, sincere counsel to those in authority, and adherence to the community; for their supplication encompasses those behind them."
"619","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Sulayman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aban, from his father, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever makes this world his intention, Allah Almighty scatters his affair upon him, places his poverty before his eyes, and nothing of this world comes to him except what was written for him. And whoever makes the Hereafter his intention, Allah Almighty places his richness in his heart, gathers his affair for him, and this world comes to him humbled."
"620","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Sulayman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aban, from his father, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Thabit saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: May Allah brighten a man who hears a hadith from us, memorizes it, and conveys it; for many a bearer of understanding carries it to one more understanding than him, and many a bearer of understanding is not himself understanding."
"621","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sahl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Said ibn Sinan, from Ibn al-Daylami, who said: I came to Zayd ibn Thabit, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If Allah Almighty punished the inhabitants of His heavens and the inhabitants of His earth, He would punish them without wronging them; and had He mercy on them, His mercy would be better for them than their deeds. Had you gold like Uhud and spent it in the path of Allah, it would not be accepted from you until you believe in the decree, all of it, its good and its evil; and if you die upon other than this, you will enter the Fire. Thus Abu Dawud said it, while the people narrate it from Said ibn Sinan, from Wahb ibn Khalid, from Ibn al-Daylami."
"622","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Hujr al-Madari, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The umra gift belongs to the heir - or he said: its way is the way of inheritance."
"623","Yunus narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to the lavatory, let him not cleanse himself with his right hand, nor touch his private part with his right hand."
"624","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir wrote to me, narrating to me from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call to prayer is announced, do not stand until you see me."
"625","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see that I have come."
"626","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not make nabidh of dates and raisins together; make nabidh of each of them separately."
"627","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would breathe in the vessel - or breathe three times."
"628","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in the first two rakahs of the noon and afternoon prayers, letting us hear a verse at times; he would lengthen the first rakah and shorten the second, and recite in the two rakahs of the sunset prayer."
"629","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon and mentioned jihad, preferring nothing over it except the prescribed prayer."
"630","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me, if I am killed in the path of Allah, where shall I be? He said: If you are killed in the path of Allah, patient, seeking reward, advancing and not retreating, then you are in Paradise. Then he fell silent, and we saw that revelation was descending upon him. Then he said: Where is the man? He said: Here I am. He said: Except if he has a debt upon him, for it will be taken from him; thus Jibril, peace be upon him, claimed."
"631","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah al-Ansari, from his father, that when a funeral bier was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would ask about it. If it was praised with good, he would pray over it; and if it was spoken of with evil, he would say to its people: Attend to it yourselves, and would not pray over it."
"632","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi Hassan, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him as a scout while his Companions were in pilgrim sanctity and he was not. He said: We saw a wild ass, so I borrowed a whip from them; they refused to lend me, so I snatched it from one of them and struck it and killed it. They refused to eat with me, so they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we did something and do not know what it is. They informed him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat, and feed us."
"633","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, that he set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of Hudaybiyah. My companions entered pilgrim sanctity and I did not. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on, and I was with my companions; some of them began laughing at others. I looked, and there was a wild ass. I charged it, pierced it, and pinned it down. I sought their help, and they refused to help me. We ate from it, and I feared my people would be cut off, so I rode my horse hard seeking the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I met a man from Ghifar in the depth of the night and said: Where did you leave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: At al-Suqya. I said: O Messenger of Allah, your Companions convey to you peace and the mercy of Allah, and they feared they would be cut off without you, so wait for them, O Messenger of Allah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I struck a wild ass, and I have some of it left with me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the people: Eat - while they were in pilgrim sanctity."
"634","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from Abu Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in the first two rakahs of the noon prayer the Opening of the Book and two chapters, letting us hear a verse; he would lengthen the first rakah beyond what he lengthened in the second, and in the last two the Opening of the Book. And he would recite with us in the dawn prayer, lengthening the first rakah beyond what he lengthened in the second."
"635","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, from Abu Qatadah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him pray two rakahs before he sits."
"636","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd Rabbih ibn Said al-Ansari, who said: I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman saying: I used to see a dream that would make me ill, so I mentioned that to Abu Qatadah. He said: I too used to see a dream that would make me ill, until I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The righteous dream is from Allah. When one of you sees what he loves, let him narrate it only to one he loves. And when he sees what he dislikes, upon waking let him spit to his left three times, seek refuge in Allah from its evil and from the evil of Satan, and inform no one of it; for it will not harm him."
"637","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ghaylan, from Abdullah ibn Mabad al-Zimmani, from Abu Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the fast of Ashura: I indeed hope from Allah Almighty that it expiates the year. And he said concerning the fast of the day of Arafah: I indeed hope from Allah that it expiates the year before it and the year after it."
"638","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd, Hisham, and Mahdi narrated to us - Hammad and Mahdi said: from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, and Hisham said: from Qatadah, from Ghaylan - from Abdullah ibn Mabad al-Zimmani, from Abu Qatadah, that a Bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about his fasting, and he grew angry until it was seen in his face. Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with you as Prophet. I seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah and the anger of His Messenger. Umar kept repeating that until he calmed. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say of a man who fasts the whole year? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He neither fasted nor broke fast - or he said: he neither fasted nor did he break fast. He said: O Messenger of Allah, how about one who fasts two days and breaks one? He said: And who can bear that? He said: O Messenger of Allah, how about one who breaks two days and fasts one? He said: I wish I were given strength for that. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say of fasting Monday? He said: That is a day on which I was born, and on which revelation was sent down to me. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say of a man who fasts one day and breaks one? He said: That is the fast of my brother Dawud. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say of fasting the day of Ashura? He said: I indeed hope from Allah that it expiates the year. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say of fasting the day of Arafah? He said: I indeed hope from Allah Almighty that it expiates the year before it and the year after it."
"639","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dug the Trench, the people would carry one brick at a time, while Ammar, ill from an ailment he had, carried two bricks at a time. Abu Said said: My companions narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would shake the dust from his head, saying: Woe to you, O son of Sumayyah, the rebellious party will kill you. This hadith was also narrated from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, from Abu Qatadah."
"640","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uqbah al-Hadrami, from Ulayy ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of horses is the black with white on the forehead and upper lip, jet black, with white legs, free on the right side; and if not jet black, then a dark bay of this color."
"641","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Dirham al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Kab ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Azdi narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Qatadah al-Ansari, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while we were building the mosque, and said: Widen it and you will fill it."
"642","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, from Abu Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would lead the people in prayer - meaning the people - while carrying Umamah, the daughter of Abu al-As, borne upon his neck. When he bowed he put her down, and when he rose he lifted her."
"643","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed me, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud al-Badri, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I pray behind so-and-so, and he lengthens the prayer until I am sometimes late. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grew angry, an anger the like of which I never saw him in admonition, then said: There are among you those who repel people. Whoever leads the people in prayer, let him lighten the prayer for them; for among them are the weak, the aged, and the one with a need."
"644","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, who said: I heard Abu Wail narrating from Abu Masud al-Badri, who said: A man among us nicknamed Abu Shuayb prepared food for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: Come, you and five with you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you permit me a sixth?"
"645","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, who said: I heard Abu Wail narrating from Abu Masud al-Badri, who said: We would carry loads for hire, and a man would come with a great charity and be called a show-off, and a man would come with half a sa. Then this verse was revealed: Those who find fault with the voluntary givers among the believers in charities - to His words: a painful punishment."
"646","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Amr al-Shaybani narrating from Abu Masud al-Badri, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a haltered she-camel as charity. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: For you on the Day of Resurrection are seven hundred haltered she-camels in return for it."
"647","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, who said: I heard Abu Amr al-Shaybani narrating from Abu Masud, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Provide me a mount, for my beast has broken down. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go to so-and-so and ask him. He went to him and asked him, and he provided him a mount. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guides to good has the like of the reward of its doer - or he said: its worker."
"648","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, who said: I heard Umarah ibn Umayr narrating from Abu Mamar al-Azdi, from Abu Masud al-Badri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of a man who does not straighten his spine - or he said: his back - in bowing and prostration does not suffice."
"649","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud al-Badri, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would straighten our shoulders - meaning in prayer - saying: Stand straight, and differ not, lest your hearts differ; and let those of understanding and reason be nearest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them. Abu Masud said: Today you differ far more."
"650","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abu Masud al-Badri, who said: A hadith reached me from him, so I met him while he was circumambulating the House and asked him. He narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the last two verses of Surat al-Baqarah in a night, they suffice him."
"651","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Yazid narrating from Abu Masud al-Badri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man spends upon his family, seeking reward for it, it is charity for him. He said: I said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"652","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Abu Masud al-Badri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray witr at the beginning of the night, its middle, and its end."
"653","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Qays, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Can none of you manage to recite a third of the Quran every night? We said: And who can bear that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Say: He is Allah, the One - is a third of the Quran."
"654","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Raja al-Zubaydi, who said: I heard Aws ibn Damaj narrating from Abu Masud al-Badri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people are led by the foremost of them in recitation of the Book of Allah and the earliest of them in recitation. If they are equal in recitation, then the earliest of them in emigration; if equal in emigration, then the eldest in age. Lead not a man in his house nor in his authority, and sit not upon his honored seat except by his permission - or he said: except he permit you."
"655","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from al-Qasim ibn Ubaydullah, from Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, from Abu Masud al-Badri, who said: We entered a house with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: This authority will remain among you, and you its rulers, so long as you do not commit new deeds. When you commit them, Allah Almighty will set over you the worst of His creation, and they will peel you as the stick is peeled. Abu Dawud said: meaning carved as the stick is carved."
"656","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Salim al-Barrad, who said: Abu Masud said to us: Shall I not pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? We said: Yes indeed. He said: He prayed with us four rakahs, the noon or afternoon prayer, placing his hands upon his knees and spreading his fingers. Then he raised his head and stood straight until everything of him settled. He did that until he completed his prayer. Then he said: Such was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"657","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Abu Masud al-Badri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: From what people have retained of the words of the first prophethood: when you feel no shame, do what you wish."
"658","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Usury is only in deferment."
"659","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mihran, he said: Umayr, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to me, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Kabah, and he saw images. He called for a bucket of water, I brought it to him, and he began erasing them, saying: May Allah destroy a people who depict what they do not create."
"660","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that he poured forth with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would go at a gentle trot; when he came to a gap he would hasten."
"661","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Usamah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to raid Ubna in the morning and burn."
"662","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Usamah, who said: I charged a man and he said: There is no god but Allah, so I drove the sword into him and killed him. He said to me: O Usamah, what will you do with There is no god but Allah on the Day of Resurrection? He repeated it many times until I wished I had not embraced Islam except at that hour."
"663","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, his maternal uncle, from Kurayb, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with gloom upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter with you? He said: Jibril promised me and I have not seen him for three days. A dog appeared, coming out of one of the houses, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered it killed. Then Jibril appeared, and he said: O Jibril, when you promised me you used to come to me, so what is with you now? He said: We enter no house in which there is a dog or images."
"664","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zibriqan, from Zuhrah, who said: We were sitting with Zayd ibn Thabit, and they sent to Usamah ibn Zayd asking him about the middle prayer. He said: It is the noon prayer; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray it at midday heat."
"665","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Shubah, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: I rode behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Arafah to Muzdalifah. He came upon a mountain path, dismounted, passed water, then did not pray until he came to Muzdalifah."
"666","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, who said: It reached me from Amir ibn Sad, whom I did not meet; I met Ibrahim ibn Sad and asked him, and he informed me that he heard Usamah ibn Zayd narrating to Sad that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the plague: When it falls in a land and you are in it, do not leave it; and when it is in a land and you are not in it, do not enter it."
"667","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Budayl narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever does not inherit from the Muslim, nor the Muslim from the disbeliever."
"668","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban narrated to him that the freedman of Qudamah ibn Mazun narrated to him that the freedman of Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to him that Usamah ibn Zayd would ride to property in Wadi al-Qura, fasting Mondays and Thursdays. I said to him: Do you fast though you have grown old and thin? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasting Monday and Thursday, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you fast Monday and Thursday? He said: Deeds are presented on Monday and Thursday."
"669","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Iyad, the in-law of Usamah, narrated to me, from Usamah, that a man came from the countryside, sickness seized him, and he returned. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hope its pass will not overlook us - meaning the pass of Medina."
"670","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Usamah, who said: I passed by Ali and al-Abbas while they were sitting in the mosque, and they said: O Usamah, seek permission for us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: O Messenger of Allah, here are Ali and al-Abbas seeking permission. He said: Do you know what brought them? I said: No, by Allah, I do not know. He said: But I know what brought them. He permitted them, they entered, greeted, then sat and said: O Messenger of Allah, which of your family is dearest to you? He said: Fatimah, daughter of Muhammad."
"671","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Kulthum al-Khuzai, from Usamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the illness in which he died: Bring my Companions in to me. They entered upon him while he was wrapped in a Mafari cloak, and said: May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"672","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from al-Shabi, who said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me that he poured forth with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Arafah, and his mount did not lift a foreleg at dawn until he came to Muzdalifah."
"673","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah, Thabit Abu Zayd, and others narrated to us, all from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that a daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to him that her son was dying and she wished him to come to her. He sent back greetings of peace, saying: To Allah belongs what He takes and what He gives, and everything with Him is for an appointed term; let her be patient and seek reward. She sent the messenger back, adjuring him that he must come. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, with Muadh ibn Jabal, Sad, and Ubayy ibn Kab with him. The boy was lifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while his soul rattled in his chest. The eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) overflowed, and Sad said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: This is mercy which Allah places in the hearts of whom He wills of His servants; and Allah Almighty shows mercy only to the merciful among His servants."
"674","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: A necklace of Aishah, of onyx from Zafar, was lost on one of the journeys of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Aishah was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on that journey. Aishah searched for her necklace until night grew dark. Abu Bakr came, grew angry at her, and said: You have detained the people in a place with no water. Then the verse of the clean earth was revealed. Abu Bakr came and said: You are, by Allah, O my daughter - as far as I knew - blessed. Ubaydullah said: Ammar used to narrate that the people that day began wiping the earth with their palms, wiping their faces with them, then returning and striking another blow, wiping their hands with them to the shoulders and armpits, then praying. Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Ammar."
"675","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, having heard Dharr ibn Abdullah narrating from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, who said: A man came to Umar and mentioned that he had been on a journey, became ritually impure, and found no water. He said: He should not pray. Ammar said: Do you not remember, O Commander of the Faithful, when you and I were in a detachment and became ritually impure and found no water? As for you, you did not pray; as for me, I rolled in the dust and prayed. When we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we mentioned that to him. He said to you: As for you, you should not have left the prayer; and as for you, O Ammar, you should not have rolled as the beast rolls. It would have sufficed you - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the earth with his hand to the dust, then said thus, blew into it, and wiped his face and his hands to the joint - and there is no mention in it of the forearms."
"676","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Dharr narrating from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, that a man came to Umar - and he mentioned something similar."
"677","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Najiyah, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: I became ritually impure while among the camels and found no water, so I rolled as the beast rolls. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Dry ablution would have sufficed you."
"678","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Salamah ibn Muhammad, from Ammar ibn Yasir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The natural disposition is rinsing the mouth, sniffing water, the toothstick, trimming the mustache, paring the nails, plucking the armpit, shaving the pubic hair, washing after relieving oneself, circumcision, and washing the finger joints."
"679","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: A man from the family of Sahl ibn Hunayf narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ammar, from Ammar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No shameless pimp enters Paradise."
"680","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, having heard Abdullah ibn Salamah saying: I saw Ammar ibn Yasir on the day of Siffin, an old dark man, with a spear in his hand that trembled. He looked at Amr ibn al-As, in whose hand was the banner, and said: This is indeed a banner I fought with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three times. By Allah, had they struck us until they brought us to the palm branches of Hajar, I would know that our party of reform is upon the truth and they upon misguidance."
"681","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from Husayn ibn Qabisah, from Ammar ibn Yasir - raised to the Prophet - who said: The double-faced one in this world will on the Day of Resurrection have two faces in the Fire. Abu Nuaym and others narrated this hadith from Sharik, from al-Rukayn, from Nuaym ibn Hanzalah, from Ammar."
"682","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Hassan ibn Bilal, who said: I saw Ammar perform ablution, running his fingers through his beard, and saying: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"683","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: I came to my family from a journey and they smeared me with saffron. In the morning I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him, but he did not welcome me nor smile at me, saying: Go and wash this off yourself. I washed it off, then came, with some of it remaining upon me; I greeted him, but he did not welcome me nor smile at me, saying: Go and wash this off yourself. I washed it off, then came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), greeted him, and he returned my greeting, welcomed me, and said: The angels do not attend the funeral of a disbeliever with good, nor one smeared with saffron, nor one in ritual impurity. And he permitted one in ritual impurity, when he wishes to eat or sleep, to perform ablution."
"684","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: A companion of ours narrated to us from Ammar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of my nation is like the rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."
"685","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, who said: Qays ibn Ubad narrated to me, saying: I said to Ammar: O Abu al-Yaqzan, tell me, this affair you undertook by your own judgment, or something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon you? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon us nothing except something he enjoined upon the people."
"686","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl al-Anazi, that Ammar, may Allah be pleased with him, was carrying with them - meaning stones - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to you, O son of Sumayyah, the rebellious party will kill you. Abd al-Warith narrated this hadith from Abu al-Tayyah, from Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Ammar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to you, O son of Sumayyah."
"687","Abu Dawud narrated to us: al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Said al-Maqburi narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham al-Makhzumi, who said: I saw Ammar ibn Yasir pray two rakahs and shorten them. I said to him - or a man said to him: O Abu al-Yaqzan, you shortened them. He said: O son of my brother, did you see me omit anything of their limits? He said: No. He said: I hastened against whispering, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man prays a prayer and has from it only half; he prays a prayer and has from it only a third; he prays a prayer and has from it only a quarter - until he reached a tenth."
"688","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from one who heard Ammar: a man mentioned Aishah before him and spoke ill of her, so he said: Be silent, disgraced and reviled. Do you harm the beloved of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"689","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Uthman, who said: I was with Salman beneath a tree; he took a dry branch from it and shook it, and its leaves fell. He said: Will you not ask me why I do this? I said: And why do you do it? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did thus, then said: O Salman, will you not ask me why I do this? I said: And why do you do this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: When the Muslim performs ablution, perfecting it, then prays the five prayers - I think he said: in congregation - his sins fall as the leaves of this tree fell. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: And establish the prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds."
"690","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from one who heard Abu Uthman, who said: Locusts were mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The most numerous of Allah's creation; I neither permit them nor forbid them. Abu al-Awwam narrated this hadith from Abu Uthman, from Salman, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"691","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: A man from the People of the Book said to a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Your companion has taught you, even teaching you how to relieve yourselves. He said: He forbade us to face the prayer direction with our private parts or turn our backs to it, and commanded us to cleanse ourselves with three stones containing neither bone nor dung. Al-Amash narrated this hadith from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Salman."
"692","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, from Zadham, from Salman, who said: In the Torah: the blessing of food is ablution before it. I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The blessing of food is ablution before it and after it."
"693","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Zayd al-Abdi narrated to us, from Abu Shurayh, from Abu Muslim, the freedman of Zayd ibn Suwan, who said: I saw Salman al-Farisi see a man wanting to remove his leather socks in ablution, and Salman commanded him to wipe over his leather socks, his turban, and his hair. Salman said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over his head-cover and his leather socks."
"694","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, having heard Abu al-Bakhtari narrating from a man of Banu Abs, who said: I accompanied Salman, and he mentioned the treasures of Kisra. He said: He who gave you and granted you and opened it for you holds back His treasury, while Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive and they would wake with neither dinar nor dirham nor a mudd of food with them - so why is that, O brother of Banu Abs? He said: Then he passed by threshing floors being winnowed, and said: He who gave you and granted you and opened it for you holds back His treasury, while Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive and they would wake with neither dinar nor dirham nor a mudd of food with them - so why is that, O brother of Banu Abs?"
"695","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Salman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Salman, hate me not, lest you leave your religion. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how could I hate you, when through you Allah has guided us? He said: You hate the Arabs, and so hate me."
"696","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from his father, from Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar, from Salman al-Khayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bathes on Friday, oils from his oil, perfumes himself from the perfume of his house, then comes to Friday prayer, separates not between two, prays, and when the imam speaks listens and is silent - he is forgiven what is between it and the next Friday."
"697","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, who said: I witnessed Jarir ibn Abdullah al-Bajali when al-Mughirah ibn Shubah perished, and heard Jarir delivering a sermon. He said: Intercede for your commander, for he loved well-being; hear and obey until a commander comes to you. As for what follows: I pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon Islam, and he stipulated upon me sincere counsel to every Muslim. By the Lord of this mosque, I am indeed sincere to you."
"698","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, who said: I heard Jarir ibn Abdullah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever shows no mercy to people, Allah shows him no mercy."
"699","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from his father, who said: We were with Jarir ibn Abdullah on a campaign and hunger struck us. Jarir wrote to Muawiyah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever shows no mercy to people, Allah shows him no mercy. Muawiyah wrote that they turn back. He said: And he provided them. Abu Ishaq said: I received a woolen cloak from what he provided them."
"700","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ubaydullah ibn Jarir, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no people among whom sins are committed, they being mightier and more numerous than the one who commits them, then they do not change it, except Allah Almighty envelops them with punishment."
"701","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Mudrik, who said: I heard Abu Zarah ibn Amr ibn Jarir narrating from Jarir ibn Abdullah al-Bajali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Jarir, make the people listen - meaning in the Farewell Pilgrimage. He said: Return not after me disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"702","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir, from Jarir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us upon a small pulpit, urging us to charity and forbidding us mutilation."
"703","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal al-Absi, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good."
"704","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Jarir ibn Abdullah al-Bajali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the collector of charity comes to you, let him not depart from you except pleased."
"705","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Jarir ibn Abdullah al-Bajali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the leather socks. Ibrahim said: This hadith used to please them, because the Islam of Jarir was after the revelation of al-Maidah."
"706","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik and Qays narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Umayr, from Zadham, from Jarir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make a niche grave and do not make a trench; for the niche is for us and the trench for others."
"707","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, who said: I heard al-Mundhir ibn Jarir narrating from his father Jarir ibn Abdullah, who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the early morning, when barefoot, naked people came, wearing striped woolen garments with openings cut in them, cloaks upon them - or he said: wearing swords - most of them from Mudar, indeed all of them from Mudar. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) change at the poverty he saw in them. He entered, then came out, commanded Bilal, who called the prayer, and he prayed the noon prayer. He delivered a sermon, saying: O people, fear your Lord who created you from a single soul - to the end of the verse. Then he said: O you who believe, fear Allah, and let each soul look to what it has put forth for tomorrow - to the end of the verse. Let a man give charity from his dinar, his dirham, his garment, his sa of wheat, his sa of dates - until he said: even half a date. A man from the Ansar came with a purse his hand could hardly lift - indeed it could not lift it - and handed it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The people followed in charities, and I saw before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two heaps of food and clothing. The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to shine as though gilded. He said: Whoever establishes in Islam a good practice has its reward and the reward of whoever acts upon it after him, without diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever establishes in Islam an evil practice bears its burden and the burden of whoever acts upon it after him, without diminishing anything from their burdens."
"708","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Muadh narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Jarir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Emigrants and the Helpers are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."
"709","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Said al-Asla, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Jarir ibn Abdullah, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the sudden glance, and he said: Lower your gaze."
"710","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ghudani, having heard al-Shabi, from Jarir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The runaway slave - no prayer is accepted from him until he returns to his masters."
"711","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, having heard Ibn Abi Layla saying: Zayd ibn Arqam would pray over our funerals, pronouncing four takbirs; one day he pronounced five. He was asked about that, and said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pronounced five."
"712","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, having heard Abu Hamzah saying: The Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, every people has followers, and we have all followed you; supplicate Allah for us that He make our followers from among us. He did so and supplicated for them. Amr said: I related that to Ibn Abi Layla, and he said: Zayd ibn Arqam claimed that."
"713","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, having heard Ibn Abi Layla saying: We would sit with Zayd ibn Arqam, saying: Narrate to us, narrate to us. He would say: We have grown old and forgotten, and narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is grave."
"714","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hamzah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are not one part of a hundred thousand - or seventy thousand - parts of those who come to my Pool; and they were on that day eight or nine hundred."
"715","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hamzah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The first to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Ali."
"716","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, having heard al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These privies are attended by devils; when one of you comes to the lavatory, let him say: I seek refuge in Allah from the male and female devils."
"717","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, having heard al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar."
"718","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, that Anas lost sons, so Zayd ibn Arqam wrote to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar."
"719","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I said to Zayd ibn Arqam: How many campaigns did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fight? He said: Nineteen campaigns."
"720","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I said to Zayd ibn Arqam: How many campaigns did you fight with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Seventeen campaigns."
"721","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I said to Zayd ibn Arqam: What was the first campaign the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fought? He said: Dhu al-Ushayrah, or Dhu al-Usayrah."
"722","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Abi Ramlah al-Shami, who said: I witnessed Muawiyah asking Zayd ibn Arqam: Did you witness with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two festivals coinciding on one day? He said: Yes. He said: What did he do? He said: He prayed the festival prayer, then permitted regarding Friday, saying: Whoever wishes to pray, let him pray."
"723","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from a man, from Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to treat pleurisy with Indian aloeswood and oil."
"724","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam, that he saw people sitting with a storyteller; when the sun rose they hastened to the pillars to pray. Zayd ibn Arqam said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of the penitent is when the young camels burn with heat."
"725","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me, he said: I heard Abu al-Minhal saying: I asked Zayd ibn Arqam and al-Bara ibn Azib about currency exchange. I would ask one of them, and he would say: Ask the other, for he is better than me. I asked them both, and they narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling gold for silver on credit."
"726","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Abdullah al-Shami, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah delivering a sermon, saying: O people of Sham, al-Ansari — meaning Zayd ibn Arqam — narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will always remain a group of my ummah fighting upon the truth until the command of Allah comes, and I consider you to be them, O people of Sham."
"727","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he said: I heard Maymun ibn Abi Shabib narrating from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever narrates a hadith from me while he thinks it is false, then he is one of the liars."
"728","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Thabit Abu Zayd — or someone else — narrated to us from Asim al-Ahwal, from Bakr, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: There are two matters about which I do not ask anyone among the people: the prayer of a man behind a man from among his subjects, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray behind Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf; and wiping over the leather socks, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over them."
"729","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from his father, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped the outer part of his leather socks."
"730","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik, Abu Awanah, Qays, and Shayban narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray until his feet swelled. He said: It was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you do this while Allah has forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Should I not be a grateful slave?"
"731","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: When Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, the sun eclipsed, so the people said: The sun has eclipsed due to the death of Ibrahim. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said: O people, the sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; so when that happens, pray until it clears."
"732","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah led us in prayer and stood up in the first two rak'ahs, so they said Subhan Allah to him, but he continued in his prayer. When he finished, he prostrated two prostrations then gave the salutation, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did likewise."
"733","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed me, he said: I heard Ibrahim narrating from Ubayd ibn Nadlah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that a man from Hudhayl had two wives, and one of them struck the other with a tent pole and caused her to miscarry. He said: Do you hold liable one who neither ate nor drank nor cried out nor uttered a sound at birth? It was said: Is it rhymed speech like the rhymed speech of the Age of Ignorance? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged in it a ghurrah — a male or female slave — and placed it upon the paternal relatives of the woman."
"734","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Aqqar ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has not truly relied upon Allah who seeks ruqyah or cauterization."
"735","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, he said: Abu Awn al-Thaqafi Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah informed me, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man with a long mustache, so he called for a siwak and a blade, placed the siwak beneath the mustache, and trimmed over it."
"736","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb al-Thaqafi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe over the turban and the leather socks."
"737","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Tu'mah ibn Amr al-Ja'fari narrated to us from Umar ibn Bayan, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells wine, let him also cut up pigs for sale."
"738","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Fadalah narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said — and I do not know it except as raised to the Prophet: The rider stays behind the funeral procession, and the one walking may be wherever he wishes of it: in front of it nearby, or to its right nearby, or to its left nearby."
"739","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Fadalah narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Jubayr ibn Hayyah, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said — and I do not consider it except as raised to the Prophet, he said: The miscarried fetus is prayed over, and supplication is made for its parents for forgiveness and mercy."
"740","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Fadalah narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from his father, he said: We set out with al-Nu'man ibn Muqarrin until we reached al-Ilj Dhu al-Hajib. They sent to us: Send to me a man so I may speak to him. He said: The people on that day chose al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. My father said: It is as if I am looking at a one-eyed man with his shield, and behold, it was al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. We reached al-Ilj and he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent among us a Prophet whom Allah promised victory; whatever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us of, we found it exactly as he informed us."
"741","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed me, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib saying: The first who came to us in Madinah — meaning in the emigration — were Mus'ab ibn Umayr and Ibn Umm Maktum, and they used to teach the Quran. Then Sa'd, Bilal, and Ammar came. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab came with twenty men. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and I never saw the people of Madinah rejoice at anything as they rejoiced at the arrival of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the slave girls in the streets were saying: The Messenger of Allah has come! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not arrive until I had already recited: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: By the night when it covers, among the surahs of al-Mufassal."
"742","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara saying: When this verse was revealed: Not equal are those believers who sit at home, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Zayd ibn Thabit and called for a shoulder blade to write it upon it, and Ibn Umm Maktum came and mentioned his disability, so this verse was revealed: Except those with disability."
"743","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara saying: The people obtained donkeys on the day of Khaybar — meaning domestic donkeys — so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a caller who announced: Overturn the cooking pots."
"744","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Umar ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara — and a man said to him: O Abu Umarah, did you flee from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn? Al-Bara said: But the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not flee. Hawazin were a people of archers; when we met them and charged at them they fled, so the people turned to the spoils while they faced us with arrows and the people fled. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on that day with Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith holding the bridle of the mule, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon his white mule, and the Prophet saying: I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib."
"745","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a man from the Ansar that when he goes to his bed he should say: O Allah, I have submitted myself to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affair to You, and laid my back against You, out of hope and fear of You; there is no refuge nor escape from You except to You; I believe in Your Book which You sent down and Your Messenger whom You sent. He said: If he dies, he dies upon the fitrah."
"746","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went to his bed, placed his hand beneath his cheek and said: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your slaves."
"747","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara saying: A silk garment was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they began touching it and marveling at its softness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A handkerchief among the handkerchiefs of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh in Paradise is softer than this."
"748","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib — he said: I said: Did you hear it from him? He said: No — that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon people sitting in the road and said: If you must do so, then return the greeting of peace, help the oppressed, and guide the way."
"749","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Trench digging with us, until I saw the dust had covered the whiteness of his belly — or he said: his hair — and he was saying — Shu'bah said in his narration: My memory, and in the written copy he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Abayna, Abayna, raising his voice with it."
"750","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made peace with the polytheists of Quraysh, he wrote between them a document: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), has agreed upon. They said: If we knew you were the Messenger of Allah we would not have fought you! He said to Ali: Erase it, but he refused, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) erased it with his hand and wrote: This is what Muhammad ibn Abdullah has agreed upon. They stipulated upon him that they would stay three days and would not enter Makkah with weapons except julubban al-silah. Shu'bah said: I said to Abu Ishaq: What is julubban al-silah? He said: The sword in its scabbard or with what is in it."
"751","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: While a man was reciting Surah al-Kahf at night, he saw his riding animal becoming restless — or he said: his horse becoming restless — then he looked and behold, something like a haze — or he said: like a cloud. He mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: That is the tranquility which descended for the Quran, or which came down upon the Quran."
"752","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: When the prohibition of wine was revealed, they said: What about those who used to drink it before it was prohibited? Then this verse was revealed: There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they consumed."
"753","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: al-Rabi ibn al-Bara ibn Azib informed me from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he returned from a journey, would say: Returning, repenting, worshipping, to our Lord praising."
"754","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: The Ansar, when they returned from a journey, a man would not enter from the direction of his door, so this verse was revealed: And righteousness is not that you enter houses from their backs, but righteousness is in one who fears Allah; and enter houses from their doors."
"755","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Ansari delivering a sermon, saying: Al-Bara ibn Azib — who was not a liar — narrated to me that when they prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and raised their heads from bowing, none of them would prostrate until they saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating, then they would prostrate."
"756","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, who heard al-Bara saying: I was deemed too young along with Ibn Umar on the day of Badr."
"757","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, he prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months. Then this verse was revealed to him: So turn your face toward al-Masjid al-Haram. It was revealed while some people were praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis, and when they heard it while in prayer, they turned their faces toward the Ka'bah while still in prayer."
"758","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: I took part in fifteen expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"759","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of medium height, wide between the shoulders, the greatest and most handsome of people; his hair reached his ears, upon him was a red garment, and I never saw anything more handsome than him."
"760","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik and Hudayj narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: Some people died while praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis, so they said: What about our companions who died while praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis? Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: And Allah would never let your faith go to waste — meaning your prayer toward Bayt al-Maqdis."
"761","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I saw the whiteness of the armpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was prostrating."
"762","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Waki' narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fighting the enemy when a man covered in iron came. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) presented Islam to him and he embraced Islam. He said: Which deed is best that I may do it? He said: Fight the people from whom you have come. So he fought them until he was killed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He did little and was rewarded much."
"763","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Abdullah ibn Jubayr over the archers of the people on the day of Uhud, and they were fifty men, and said to them: Stay in your place, do not leave it, even if you see the birds snatching us. Al-Bara said: By Allah, I saw the women with their anklets visible, their garments loosened, climbing the mountain. When what happened happened and the people were plundering, they left. Abdullah ibn Jubayr, their commander, said: What will you do with the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? But they went on, and what happened happened. When night came, Abu Sufyan ibn Harb came and said: Is Muhammad among you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not answer him. Then he said: Is Muhammad among you? They did not answer him. Then he said: Is Muhammad among you? a third time, and they did not answer him. Then he said: Is the son of Abu Quhafah among you? They did not answer him — he said it three times. Then he said: Is the son of al-Khattab among you? He said it three times and they did not answer him. He said: As for these, you have been relieved of them. Umar could not restrain himself and said: You have lied, O enemy of Allah; here is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr and I are alive, and for you from us is an evil day. He said: A day for the day of Badr, and war goes by turns. And he said: Exalted be Hubal! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Answer him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall we say? He said: Say: Allah is Most High and Most Sublime. He said: We have al-Uzza and you have no Uzza! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Answer him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall we say? He said: Say: Allah is our Protector and you have no protector. Then Abu Sufyan said: You will see among the people a mutilation that I did not command, and it did not displease me."
"764","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: It was said to al-Bara: Was the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like a sword? He said: No, but like the moon."
"765","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umrah in Dhu al-Qa'dah."
"766","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit al-Ansari, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the Ansar: None loves them except a believer and none hates them except a hypocrite; whoever loves them, Allah loves him, and whoever hates them, Allah hates him. He said: So I said to Adi: Who narrated to you from al-Bara? He said: Al-Bara himself informed me."
"767","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit, he said: I heard al-Bara saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when his son Ibrahim died: He has a nursing mother in Paradise."
"768","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Adi informed me, he said: I heard al-Bara saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hassan ibn Thabit: Lampoon them — meaning the polytheists, or he said: attack them — and Jibril is with you."
"769","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit, he said: I heard al-Bara and Ibn Abi Awfa narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys, so the cooking pots were overturned."
"770","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit, he said: I heard al-Bara saying: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing al-Hasan upon his shoulder, and he said: Whoever loves me, let him love him."
"771","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit, who heard al-Bara saying: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he recited in Maghrib in the second rak'ah: By the fig and the olive."
"772","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from al-A'mash, from Abdullah, a freed slave of Quraysh, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about ablution from camel meat, so he commanded it; and he was asked about prayer in the resting places of camels, so he forbade it."
"773","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Abdullah, the freed slave of Quraysh, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about ablution from sheep meat, so he permitted ablution from it; and he was asked about prayer in their resting places, so he permitted it."
"774","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam informed me that when Matar ibn Najiyah gained control over Kufah, he ordered Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah to lead the people in prayer, so he led the people in prayer, and when he raised his head from bowing he would prolong the standing. I mentioned it to Ibn Abi Layla, who narrated from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — when he prayed, then bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, and when he prostrated, and when he raised his head from prostration, between the two prostrations — was nearly equal in length."
"775","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, having heard Ibn Abi Layla narrating from al-Bara, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate qunut in the dawn prayer and the sunset prayer."
"776","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beautify the Quran with your voices. Shu'bah said: I forgot this wording until al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim reminded me of it."
"777","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Talhah al-Yami, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise. He said: Short though your sermonizing is, you have posed a broad question! Free a soul and liberate a neck. He said: O Messenger of Allah, are they not the same? He said: No; freeing a soul is that you do it alone, and liberating a neck is that you help in its price; and the freely-given milch animal, and showing kindness to the unjust blood relative. He said: And whoever cannot do that? He said: Then feed the hungry and give drink to the thirsty. He said: And if I cannot? He said: Enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong. He said: And whoever cannot do that? He said: Then restrain your tongue except from good."
"778","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I asked Talhah ibn Musarrif about this hadith more than twenty times — had it been someone else he would have said thirty times. He said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah narrating from al-Bara ibn Azib that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants a gift of silver — or he said: silver — or guides through a narrow passage, or gives milk to drink, it will be for him like the freeing of a soul or a neck; and whoever says: There is no god but Allah, alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Capable, ten times, they will be for him like the freeing of a soul or a neck."
"779","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Talhah ibn Musarrif, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah narrating from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to us when we stood for prayer and wipe our shoulders and chests, saying: Do not differ, lest your hearts differ; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His angels send blessings upon the first row — or he said: the foremost rows."
"780","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Bara, that when the son of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Ibrahim, died, he said: He has a nursing mother who nurses him in Paradise."
"781","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Zubayd, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi narrating from al-Bara that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered the sermon on the day of sacrifice and said: The first thing we begin with on this day of ours is that we pray, then return and slaughter; whoever does that has attained our sunnah, and whoever slaughtered before the prayer, it is only meat he presented to his family, having nothing to do with the sacrifice. My maternal uncle Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, who had slaughtered before the prayer, stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a young goat dearer to me than a grown sheep! He said: Sacrifice it, but it will never suffice for anyone after you."
"782","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he said: I heard Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from al-Bara, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a man, when he takes his bed at night, to say: O Allah, I have submitted myself to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affair to You, and laid my back against You, out of hope and fear of You; there is no refuge nor escape from You except to You; I believe in Your Book which You sent down and Your Messenger whom You sent. He said: If he dies, he dies upon the fitrah."
"783","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from al-Bara, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding His saying: Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word — he said: In the grave when he is questioned."
"784","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Ash'ath, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Suwayd ibn Muqarrin informed me, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us with seven and forbade us seven: he commanded us to visit the sick, follow funeral processions, return the greeting of peace, bless the sneezer, fulfill the oath of one who swears, help the oppressed, and accept the invitation of one who invites; and he forbade us the gold ring — or he said: the gold signet — vessels of gold and silver, the saddle cloth of silk, garments of qassi, istabraq, silk, and brocade."
"785","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us from Layth, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Mu'awiyah ibn Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Do you know which handle of faith is firmest? We said: Prayer. He said: Prayer is good, but it is not that. We said: Fasting, and he said the same, until we mentioned jihad, and he said the same. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The firmest handle of faith is love for the sake of Allah and hatred for the sake of Allah."
"786","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you prostrate, place your hand and raise your elbows."
"787","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Ubayd ibn Fayruz saying: I asked al-Bara ibn Azib what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked or forbade regarding sacrificial animals? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us like this — and my hand is shorter than his hand — and said: Four do not suffice: the one-eyed whose blindness is evident, the sick whose sickness is evident, the lame whose lameness is evident, and the broken-boned that has no marrow. I said: I dislike there being a defect in the tooth or a defect in the horn or a defect in the ear. He said: What you dislike, leave it, but do not forbid it to anyone."
"788","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he said: I heard Abu al-Minhal saying: I asked al-Bara ibn Azib and Zayd ibn Arqam about currency exchange. I would ask one of them and he would say: Ask the other, for he is better than me and more knowledgeable. So I asked them both and they narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling silver for gold on credit."
"789","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hushaym and Abu Awanah narrated to us from Abu Balj, from Ziyad Abu al-Hakam al-Bajali, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a Muslim meets his brother and shakes his hand, and they praise Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and seek His forgiveness, Allah forgives them both."
"790","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: I heard Abu Juhayfah narrating from al-Bara, he said: Abu Burdah slaughtered before the prayer, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Replace it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing but a young goat better than a grown sheep! He said: Put it in its place, but it will never suffice for anyone after you."
"791","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Zadhad, from al-Bara ibn Azib. Abu Dawud said: And Amr ibn Thabit narrated it to us, having heard it from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Zadhad, from al-Bara ibn Azib — and the narration of Abu Awanah is the more complete of the two. Al-Bara said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the funeral of a man from the Ansar. We reached the grave before the niche was dug. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and we sat around him as though birds were upon our heads — Amr ibn Thabit said: perched, and Abu Awanah did not say it — and he began raising his gaze, looking to the sky, and lowering his gaze, looking to the earth. Then he said: I seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave, saying it repeatedly. Then he said: When the believing slave is at the threshold of the Hereafter and cut off from this world, an angel comes and sits at his head, saying: Come out, O tranquil soul, to forgiveness from Allah and His pleasure. His soul comes out and flows as the drop of the waterskin flows — Amr said in his narration, which Abu Awanah did not say: even though you may see otherwise — and angels from Paradise descend, white-faced as though their faces were the sun, with shrouds from the shrouds of Paradise and embalming perfume from its perfume, and they sit as far as the eye can see. When the angel seizes it, they do not leave it in his hand for the blink of an eye — and that is His saying, Mighty and Majestic: Our messengers take him, and they do not fall short. He said: His soul comes out like the sweetest scent ever found, and the angels ascend with him. They do not pass any host between heaven and earth except they say: What is this spirit? It is said: So-and-so — by his best names — until they reach with him the gate of the lowest heaven and it is opened for him, and those nearest to Allah in every heaven escort him, until he is brought to the seventh heaven. He says: Write his record in Illiyyun — And what will make you know what Illiyyun is? A written register, witnessed by those brought near — so his record is written in Illiyyun. Then it is said: Return him to the earth, for I promised them that from it I created them, into it I shall return them, and from it I shall bring them out another time. He is returned to the earth and his spirit is restored to his body. Two angels come to him, stern in rebuke; they rebuke him and seat him, saying: Who is your Lord? What is your religion? He says: My Lord is Allah and my religion is Islam. They say: What do you say about this man who was sent among you? He says: He is the Messenger of Allah. They say: How do you know? He says: He came to us with clear proofs from our Lord, so I believed in him and affirmed him. He said: And that is His saying, Mighty and Majestic: Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter. He said: A caller from heaven calls out: My slave has spoken the truth, so clothe him from Paradise, spread for him from it, and show him his dwelling in it. He is clothed from Paradise, it is spread for him from it, he is shown his dwelling in it, his grave is widened for him as far as the eye can see, and his deed is presented to him in the form of a man with a handsome face, sweet scent, and fine clothes, saying: Rejoice in what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has prepared for you; rejoice in the pleasure of Allah and Gardens wherein is lasting bliss. He says: May Allah give you glad tidings of good; who are you? Your face is the face that has come with good. He says: This is your day which you were promised, and the matter which you were promised; I am your righteous deed. By Allah, I knew you only as swift in obedience to Allah and slow to disobey Allah, so may Allah reward you with good. He says: O Lord, establish the Hour so I may return to my family and wealth. He said: And if he is wicked, and is at the threshold of the Hereafter and cut off from this world, an angel comes and sits at his head, saying: Come out, O wicked soul; receive tidings of the wrath and anger of Allah. Black-faced angels descend with coarse cloths. When the angel seizes it, they stand and do not leave it in his hand for the blink of an eye. He said: It becomes submerged in his body, and he extracts it, tearing with it the veins and nerves, like a large skewer with many prongs in wet wool. It is taken from the angel and comes out like the foulest stench ever found. It does not pass any host between heaven and earth except they say: What is this wicked spirit? They say: So-and-so — by his worst names — until they reach the lowest heaven and it is not opened for him. He says: Return him to the earth; I promised them that from it I created them, into it I shall return them, and from it I shall bring them out another time. He said: He is cast down from heaven. He said: He recited this verse: And whoever associates with Allah, it is as though he had fallen from the sky. He said: He is returned to the earth, his spirit is restored in him, and two angels come to him, stern in rebuke; they rebuke him and seat him, saying: Who is your Lord? What is your religion? He says: I do not know. They say: What do you say about this man who was sent among you? He cannot recall his name, saying: I do not know; I heard the people saying that. He said: It is said: You neither knew — and his grave is constricted upon him until his ribs interlock, and his deed is presented to him in the form of a man with an ugly face, foul scent, and ugly clothes, saying: Receive tidings of punishment from Allah and His wrath. He says: Who are you? Your face is the face that has come with evil. He says: I am your wicked deed. By Allah, I knew you only as slow to obey Allah and swift to disobey Allah. Amr said in his narration from al-Minhal, from Zadhad, from al-Bara, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A deaf and dumb angel is appointed over him with a mallet — had a mountain been struck with it, it would have become dust — or he said: crumbled bones — and he strikes him with it a blow heard by all creatures except the two weighty beings; then the spirit is restored in him and he strikes him another blow."
"792","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turn Ma'iz away twice, then order him to be stoned."
"793","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering the sermon, saying: Before the Hour there will be liars — then he said a word I did not understand, so I said to my father: What did he say? He said: Beware of them."
"794","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This religion will always remain established; a band of Muslims will fight for it until the Hour is established."
"795","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering the sermon standing, then sitting, then standing and delivering the sermon."
"796","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I said to Jabir ibn Samurah: What would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do when he prayed the dawn prayer? He said: He would sit in his sitting place until the sun rose."
"797","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir saying: I saw the Seal upon the shoulder of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like an egg."
"798","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Simak, he said: I heard Jabir saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the funeral of Ibn al-Dahdahah, while he was upon a horse that was prancing with him, and we were hurrying around him."
"799","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays claimed from Simak ibn Harb, narrating from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only mounted the horse after finishing his burial."
"800","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: They used to call Madinah Yathrib, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named it Taybah."
"801","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Simak, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah, mentioning the gray hair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: When he oiled it, it was not seen, and when he did not oil it, it was visible."
"802","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Zuhr and Asr: By the night when it covers, and the like of it, and would recite in the dawn prayer longer than that."
"803","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Ma'iz ibn Malik was stoned — a short man with muscles. When he finished stoning him, he said: Whenever we go out campaigning in the cause of Allah, one of them stays behind, bleating like the bleating of a billy goat, granting one of them the handful of dates. Indeed, if Allah enables me over any of them, I shall make an example of him."
"804","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Simak informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had light-colored eyes with a reddish tinge, lean heels, and a wide mouth."
"805","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Simak ibn Harb informed me, he said: I heard Abu Thawr narrating from Jabir ibn Samurah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about ablution from sheep meat and permitted it; he was asked about prayer in the resting places of sheep — or he said: their night resting places, Abu Dawud doubted — and permitted it; he was asked about ablution from camel meat and commanded it; and he was asked about prayer in the resting places of camels and forbade it, disliking it."
"806","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Simak, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering the sermon, saying: Islam will always remain mighty until twelve caliphs — then he said a word I did not understand, so I said to my father: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say? He said: All of them from Quraysh."
"807","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned Ma'iz, and did not mention flogging."
"808","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir. Hammad said: And Sayyar ibn Salamah narrated it to me from Abu Barzah al-Aslami — one of them said: Bilal would call the adhan when the sun declined, and the other said: Bilal would call the adhan when the sun had passed its zenith."
"809","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: Bilal would not delay the adhan beyond its time, though he would sometimes delay the iqamah a little."
"810","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik and Qays narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I said to Jabir ibn Samurah: Did you sit with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; he was long in silence and little in laughter. His companions would sometimes recite poetry to one another in his presence, and things from their affairs, and they would laugh, and perhaps he would smile."
"811","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us from Simak, he said: I said to Jabir ibn Samurah: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) deliver the sermon? He said: Whoever narrates to you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered the sermon sitting, disbelieve him; I witnessed him delivering the sermon standing. I said: How was his sermon? He said: It was moderate; he would recite verses from the Book of Allah and speak words with which he admonished the people."
"812","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Zuhr like your prayer, Asr like your prayer, Maghrib like your prayer, and would delay Isha a little."
"813","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us from Simak, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in Zuhr and Asr: By the heaven and the night comer, and: By the heaven full of stars."
"814","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"815","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Simak, from Jabir, that a man had a she-camel at al-Harrah and entrusted it to a man, though it had been ill. When it was about to die, his wife said to him: If only you would slaughter it and we could eat from it! He refused, and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Do you have what suffices you? He said: No. He said: Then eat it — though it had already died. She said: We ate from its fat, meat, and grease for about twenty days. Then he met its owner, who said to him: Why did you not slaughter it? He said: I was shy before you."
"816","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not have the adhan called for the two Eids."
"817","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights."
"818","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that a man killed himself with an arrowhead, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over him."
"819","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: When we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we would sit wherever we reached."
"820","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Mu'adh narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Makkah there is a stone that used to greet me on the nights I was sent; I recognize it when I pass by it."
"821","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The white palace of Khosrau will be conquered by a band of Muslims."
"822","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us from Simak, from Jabir, he said: Bilal would call the adhan when the sun declined, sometimes delaying the iqamah a little and sometimes hastening it a little; as for the adhan, he would not delay it beyond its time."
"823","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us from Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha, from Ja'far ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to fast Ashura, urging us upon it and checking upon us regarding it. When Ramadan was made obligatory, he neither commanded us with it nor forbade us from it, nor checked upon us regarding it."
"824","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us from A'idh ibn Nasib, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointing with his finger in prayer; when he gave the salutation, I heard him saying: O Allah, I ask You for all good, what I know of it and what I do not know, and I seek refuge with You from all evil, what I know of it and what I do not know."
"825","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from al-A'mash, he said: I heard al-Musayyab ibn Rafi' narrating from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw people raising their hands and said: They have raised their hands as though they are the tails of restive horses; be still in prayer."
"826","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering the sermon on Friday, reciting from the Quran and admonishing the people."
"827","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: In the son of Adam there is a morsel of flesh; if it is sound, the rest of his body is sound, and if it is corrupt, the rest of his body is corrupt — and it is the heart."
"828","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that his father granted him a gift, wanting the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness it. He said: Have you granted all your children as you granted him? He said: No. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is your duty to be just among your children, just as it is their duty to be dutiful to you."
"829","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, may Allah have mercy on him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The example of the believers and the example of their mutual affection, love, and mercy is like the body; when part of it complains, the rest of it responds with sleeplessness and fever."
"830","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, who heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten the row until he made it like an arrow or a spear. When he thought we had learned that from him and understood it, he saw a man standing apart with his chest out of the row. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O slaves of Allah, you shall straighten your rows, or Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will cause dissension among you."
"831","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir delivering a sermon wearing a woolen garment of his, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering the sermon, saying: I warn you of the Fire — to such an extent that had a man been at such-and-such a place, he would have heard his voice."
"832","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The example of the believers is like the body; when part of it aches, the rest of it responds."
"833","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: If a man on a journey had his mount with his provisions and water upon it, and it strayed, and he climbed an elevation and looked but saw nothing; while he was like that, he saw it, with his provisions and water upon it — then Allah is more intensely joyful at the repentance of His slave than the owner of the mount is at his mount. Abu Dawud did not raise it as from Hammad, while Ibn al-Asbahani raised it from Sharik, from Simak, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"834","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in Friday prayer and the two Eids: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming?"
"835","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us from Abu Bishr, from Habib ibn Salim, that a woman came to al-Nu'man ibn Bashir and said: My husband had intercourse with my slave girl without my permission. Al-Nu'man said: I have in this a decisive judgment which I took from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): if you had not permitted him, I would stone him, and if you had permitted him, I would flog him a hundred lashes. The people said to her: Woe to you, the father of your child will be stoned! So she came and said: I had permitted him, but jealousy drove me to what I said! So he flogged him a hundred lashes."
"836","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us from Abu Bishr, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I am the most knowledgeable of people regarding the time of this prayer — meaning the last night prayer; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray it at moonset on the third night."
"837","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir delivering a sermon, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment is a man in the hollows of whose feet are two coals — or a coal — from which his brain boils."
"838","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, having heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd saying: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: You shall straighten your rows, or Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will cause dissension among you."
"839","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Asim, from Abu Qilabah, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prayed in the eclipse, bowing and prostrating twice."
"840","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Mansur, he said: I heard Dharr narrating from Yusay' al-Hadrami, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Supplication is worship. Your Lord said: Call upon Me; I will respond to you."
"841","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from Abu Azib, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no retaliation except with an iron weapon."
"842","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from Abu Azib, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: We accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard him saying: Before the Hour there will be tribulations like pieces of the dark night; a man will wake as a believer and sleep as a disbeliever, and sleep as a believer and wake as a disbeliever; peoples will sell their share of the Hereafter for a small price of this world."
"843","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah al-Aslami, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer, then a Bedouin called out for the red camel — saying it in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May you not find it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These mosques were built only for what they were built for."
"844","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the prayers with a single ablution."
"845","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, he said: Alqamah ibn Marthad narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Are there horses in Paradise? For I love them! He said: If you love that, you will be brought a horse of red ruby that will fly with you in Paradise wherever you wish. And a man said to him: I love camels; are there camels in Paradise? He said: O slave of Allah, if you are admitted to Paradise, you shall have therein what your soul desires and your eyes delight in."
"846","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted visiting graves."
"847","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he turned Ma'iz away four times."
"848","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, he said: Buraydah al-Aslami visited a dying man in Khurasan and saw sweat upon his forehead. Buraydah said: Allah is Greatest! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The believer dies with sweat upon the forehead."
"849","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from his father, from Buraydah, he said: I went out one day walking and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), thinking he intended to relieve himself, so I crossed before him until he saw me. He sent for me and I came to him; he took my hand and we walked together. A man was before us praying, making many bowings and prostrations. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you think he is showing off? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He released my hand and said: Upon you is moderate guidance, for whoever contends with this religion, it will overcome him."
"850","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us from Yahya, from Abu Qilabah, that Abu al-Malih narrated to him, he said: We were with Buraydah al-Ansari on an expedition on a cloudy day, and he said: Pray early, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say — or the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever abandons the afternoon prayer, his deed is rendered void."
"851","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Thawwab ibn Utbah al-Mahri narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Buraydah al-Aslami narrated to us from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not go out on the day of Fitr until he ate, and would not eat on the day of sacrifice until he slaughtered."
"852","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Ahmari informed me, from Ibn Buraydah al-Aslami, from his father, that a man from Khuza'ah died in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought his inheritance. He said: Look whether there is an heir. They sought but found no heir for him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hand it to the eldest of Khuza'ah."
"853","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us from Ibrahim al-Saksaki, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not know the Quran well; is there anything from the Quran that suffices? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah. Then the man turned away, then returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is for Allah; what is for me? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, grant me well-being, guide me, and provide for me. The man counted them upon his hand as ten. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for this one, he has filled his hands with good."
"854","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman al-Shaybani, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the red jar. I said: And the white? He said: I do not know."
"855","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mujalid, he said: Abu Burdah and Abdullah ibn Shaddad disputed regarding advance payment, so they sent me to Ibn Abi Awfa and I asked him. He said: We used to pay in advance in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for wheat, barley, raisins, and dates, to people who did not have it. He said: So we asked Ibn Abza and he said the same."
"856","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys."
"857","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Qays narrated to us from Ubayd ibn al-Hasan, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say in his supplication: O Allah, to You belongs praise filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever You will after that. Abu Dawud said: Qays said in his narration: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say this when he raised his head from bowing."
"858","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ya'fur, who heard Ibn Abi Awfa saying: I took part in seven expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), eating locusts with him."
"859","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah, who heard Ibn Abi Awfa saying: When people of a household brought charity, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would invoke blessings upon them. My father gave charity, so he said: O Allah, send blessings upon the family of Abu Awfa."
"860","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, having heard Ibn Abi Awfa, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — who had witnessed the Pledge of Ridwan — saying: On that day we were one thousand three hundred, and Aslam on that day were an eighth of the Emigrants."
"861","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Harish ibn Sulaym al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Talhah al-Yami narrated to us, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) make a bequest? He said: No. I said: Why did he command us with bequests while he did not bequeath? He said: He bequeathed the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"862","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Hashraj narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Jumhan narrated to us, he said: I came to Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: Who are you? He was at that time blind. I said: I am Sa'id ibn Jumhan. He said: What happened to your father? I said: The Azariqah killed him. He said: May Allah have mercy on him; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that they are the dogs of the Fire."
"863","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Firas, from Mudrik ibn Umarah, from Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A slave does not commit adultery while committing it as a believer, nor steal while stealing as a believer, nor drink wine while drinking it as a believer, nor plunder a plunder of high value as a believer."
"864","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam narrated to us from a man, from Ibn Abi Awfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise."
"865","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Ubayd ibn al-Hasan, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with this supplication: O Allah, to You belongs praise filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever You will after that. Shu'bah said: And I heard Majza'ah ibn Zahir saying: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa mentioning this supplication, adding in it: O Allah, purify me with snow, hail, and cold water; O Allah, cleanse me of sins and errors as the white garment is cleansed of filth."
"866","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim al-Hajari informed me, he said: I saw Ibn Abi Awfa at the funeral of his daughter, riding upon a mule. He passed by women wailing and said: Beware of wailing laments, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it; let one of you shed from her tears."
"867","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Ghaylan ibn Jarir al-Mi'wali, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, he said: I prayed with Imran ibn Husayn behind Ali ibn Abi Talib. When he prostrated he said Allahu Akbar, when he raised his head he said Allahu Akbar, and when he rose from the two prostrations he said Allahu Akbar. When we finished the prayer, Imran took my hand and said: This one has reminded us of the prayer of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — or he said: he led us in the prayer of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — Ghaylan doubted."
"868","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Hilal al-Adawi informed me, he said: I heard Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrating from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah have mercy on him, he said: He said to me: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith through which Allah may benefit you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Hajj and Umrah, then did not forbid it, nor did any Quran descend forbidding it; and the angels used to greet me with peace, but when I cauterized myself it ceased from me, and when I abandoned it, it returned to me."
"869","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Yazid al-Rishk, he said: I heard Mutarrif narrating from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Are the people of Paradise known from the people of the Fire? He said: Yes. He said: Then for what do the workers work? He said: Each works for what he was created for and made easy for."
"870","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Duba'i narrated to us, Yazid al-Rishk narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali in an army, and they saw something from him which they disapproved of. Four men agreed and pledged to inform the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of what Ali had done. Imran said: When we returned from a journey, we would not go to our families until we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), greeted him, and looked at him. The four men came; one of them stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not see that Ali did such-and-such? He turned away from him. Then the second stood and said the same, and he turned away from him. Then the third stood and said the same, and he turned away from him. Then the fourth stood and said the same. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is it with them and Ali! Ali is from me and I am from him, and he is the guardian of every believer after me."
"871","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization, but we were cauterized, and we neither prospered nor succeeded."
"872","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Fast the sirar of the month. Abu Dawud said: meaning after the breaking of the fast."
"873","Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, that he had two wives. He came to one of them and she said: Have you come from so-and-so, meaning his other wife? He said: No, but I was with Imran ibn Husayn, who reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fewest of the people of Paradise are women."
"874","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Ashhab, Jarir ibn Hazim, Salm ibn Zurayr, Hammad ibn Najih, and Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn and Ibn Abbas, may Allah have mercy on them, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into Paradise and most of its people were the poor, and I looked into the Fire and most of its people were women."
"875","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that an old man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Messenger of Allah, my son has died; what is my share of his inheritance? He said: A sixth for you. When he turned away, he called him back and said: Another sixth for you. When he turned away, he called him back and said: The other sixth is an extra allotment."
"876","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while on a journey, raised his voice with the two verses: O mankind, fear your Lord, up to His saying: but the punishment of Allah is severe. He said: So they urged the mounts on and knew he was about to say something. When they had gathered around him, he said: Do you know what day that is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That is a day when Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say to Adam: O Adam, rise and send forth the delegation of the Fire. He will say: My Lord, what is the delegation of the Fire? He will say: Out of every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise. So they grew despondent until none of them showed his teeth. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he said: Act and receive glad tidings; by the One in whose Hand is my soul, you are with two creations that never appear in anything but that they make it more numerous, with Gog and Magog and those who perished of the children of Adam and the children of Iblis. Act and receive glad tidings; by the One in whose Hand is my soul, you among people are but like a mole on the side of a camel or a mark on the foreleg of a beast."
"877","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Amir Salih ibn Rustum narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: Rarely did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand among us without urging us to charity and forbidding us mutilation. He said: Part of mutilation is for a man to vow to cut off his nose, and part of mutilation is for a man to vow to perform Hajj on foot. So if one of you vows to perform Hajj on foot, let him offer a sacrificial animal and ride."
"878","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and they slept, and did not wake until the sun had risen. They prayed, and said: Messenger of Allah, shall we add to our prayer? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah forbids you usury yet accepts it from you! And this hadith is also reported from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"879","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Qazaah, from al-Hasan; and Hammad ibn Salamah, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, with Hammad raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Dawud said: I do not retain it from Shubah as raised. He said: There is no jostling to outrun, no seeking advantage by position, and no shighar marriage in Islam."
"880","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanzali, from his father, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow in anger, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"881","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadrah, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakahs in Makkah and then gave the salutation, and said: O people of Makkah, complete your prayer, for we are traveling people."
"882","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, saying: Abu Jamrah informed me, saying: I heard Zahdam ibn Mudarrib reporting from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of my nation is my generation, and he mentioned something like the hadith of Hisham."
"883","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Azrah ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Uqayl narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Abu al-Aswad al-Duali, saying: Imran ibn Husayn reported to me that a man of Juhaynah or Muzaynah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Messenger of Allah, what people do, is it a matter decreed for them of a decree that preceded them, or something you brought them by which proof is established against them? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather what was decreed for them and apportioned for them of a decree that preceded. He said: Then he said: Messenger of Allah, then why do they act? He said: Act, for each is facilitated for what he was created for. And he recited this verse: By the soul and what proportioned it, then inspired it with its wickedness and its piety."
"884","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Hafs al-Laythi, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the earthen jar."
"885","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought al-Uqayli in bonds. [FLAG: obscure referent, literal]"
"886","Abu Dawud narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a man freed six slaves of his at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two, and kept four enslaved."
"887","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"888","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ransomed two men of his Companions who were in the hands of the polytheists for a captive man."
"889","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr or Asr as three rakahs and then gave the salutation. A man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ibn al-Khirbaq said: Has the prayer been shortened? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, and it was as he had said. He said: So he prayed one rakah, then gave the salutation, then prostrated two prostrations, then gave the salutation."
"890","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Abu Qilabah reported to him, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a woman of Juhaynah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while she was pregnant from adultery. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her guardian to treat her well, and said: When she delivers her burden, bring her to me. He did so. He commanded regarding her, so her garments were fastened about her, then he commanded regarding her and she was stoned. Then he prayed over her. Umar said to him: Messenger of Allah, do you pray over her when she committed adultery? He said: She has repented a repentance that, if divided among the people of Madinah, would encompass them. Have you found anything better than that she gave herself up for Allah?"
"891","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Abu Qilabah reported to him, that Abu al-Muhallab reported to him, from Imran, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother the Negus has died, so pray over him. He said: So we lined up behind him as one lines up for the dead, and we prayed over him as one prays over the dead."
"892","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who heard Abu Mirayah, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience in disobedience of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"893","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who heard Zurarah, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr with his Companions and said: Which of you recited Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High? A man said: I did. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I knew that a man was contending with me over it. Shubah said: So I said to Qatadah: As if he disliked it! He said: Had he disliked it, he would have forbidden it."
"894","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of my nation is the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people who vow but do not fulfill, betray and are not trusted, bear witness though not asked to, and obesity will spread among them."
"895","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, saying: I heard Abu al-Sawwar reporting from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty brings nothing but good. Bushayr ibn Kab said: In wisdom it is said: Part of modesty is dignity, and part of modesty is weakness! Imran said: I report to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you report to me from the scriptures!"
"896","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Rabah Abu al-Fadl narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi narrated to us, that Imran ibn Husayn reported to them, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is altogether good."
"897","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Subayh, from Ibn Sirin, who said: Weeping over the dead, that he is punished for it, was mentioned before Imran ibn Husayn. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it."
"898","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: I asked Muhammad ibn Sirin about the hadith of Imran ibn Husayn, and he said: Imran said to al-Hakam al-Ghifari, both Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do you know the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience in disobedience of Allah, Mighty and Majestic? He said: Yes. Imran said: Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great."
"899","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Uqbah ibn Khalid or Khalid ibn Uqbah, the doubt is from Abu Dawud, narrated to us, saying: Abu Raja al-Utaridi narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey. He alighted and slept, and said to Bilal: Wake us for our prayer. They did not wake except by the heat of the sun on their backs and shoulders. He said: Move on from this place. So they moved on, then alighted, and he said to Bilal: What prevented you from waking us? He said: What made you sleep made me sleep. He said: So they performed tayammum with the earth, and he commanded Bilal, who gave the call to prayer, and they prayed the two rakahs, then he stood and they prayed the morning prayer."
"900","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadrah, who said: A young man asked Imran ibn Husayn about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on journeys. He said: This youth asked me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on journeys, so retain them from me: I never traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on any journey but that he prayed two rakahs until he returned. I was present with him at Hunayn and Taif, and he prayed two rakahs. Then I performed Hajj and Umrah with him, and he prayed two rakahs, then said: O people of Makkah, complete the prayer, for we are traveling people. Then I performed Hajj and Umrah with Abu Bakr, and he prayed two rakahs, then said: O people of Makkah, complete, for we are traveling people. Then I performed Hajj and Umrah with Umar, and he prayed two rakahs, then said: Complete the prayer, for we are traveling people. Then I performed Hajj and Umrah with Uthman, and he prayed two by two rakahs, then Uthman completed the prayer."
"901","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not return after me astray, striking the necks of one another."
"902","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr informed me, saying: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, that his father wrote to him while he was in Sijistan: Do not judge between two men while you are angry, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man shall judge between two men or between two disputants while he is angry."
"903","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Yaqub, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What if Muzaynah, Juhaynah, Aslam, and Ghifar are better than Banu Tamim, Asad, Ghatfan, and Banu Amir ibn Sasah? They would be losers and ruined. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, they are better than them."
"904","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, who heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah reporting from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Muzaynah, Juhaynah, Aslam, and Ghifar are better than Banu Tamim, Asad, Ghatfan, and Banu Amir ibn Sasah."
"905","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, saying: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, who said: A man was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they praised him well. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the man: Woe to you, you have cut the neck of your companion, saying it three times. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you must praise his brother, let him say: I deem so-and-so, if he knows that of him, and I do not declare anyone pure before Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"906","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha and Salim ibn Ubaydullah ibn Salim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The two months of Eid are not deficient: Ramadan and Dhul Hijjah."
"907","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, who said: It was said: Messenger of Allah, which people are best? He said: He whose life is long and whose deeds are good. It was said: Messenger of Allah, then which people are worst? He said: He whose life is long and whose deeds are evil."
"908","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parents of the Dajjal remain thirty years without a child being born to them. Then a boy is born to them, one-eyed, most harmful and least beneficial; his eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described his father: a tall man, lean of flesh, as if his nose were a beak; and his mother a tall woman, large-breasted. Abu Bakrah said: So we heard of a newborn born in Madinah among the Jews. I and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam went and entered upon his parents, and there was the description of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in them. We said: Do you have a child? They said: We remained thirty years without a child being born to us, then a child was born to us, most harmful and least beneficial; his eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep. We went out from them and there he was, lying wrapped in a blanket in the sun, humming. He uncovered his head and said: What did you two say? We said: Did you hear? He said: I sleep, but my heart does not sleep."
"909","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, who said: We came as a delegation to Muawiyah with Ziyad, and Abu Bakrah was with us. We entered upon him, and Muawiyah said to him: Report to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); perhaps Allah will benefit us by it. He said: Yes; the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like good dreams and ask about them. A man said: Messenger of Allah, I saw a dream: I saw as if a scale was let down from the heaven, and you and Abu Bakr were weighed, and you outweighed Abu Bakr. Then Abu Bakr and Umar were weighed, and Abu Bakr outweighed Umar. Then Umar and Uthman were weighed, and Umar outweighed Uthman. Then the scale was raised! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was displeased by it, then said: A caliphate of prophethood, then Allah gives kingship to whom He wills. Muawiyah became angry and had us pushed out by our necks. Ziyad said to Abu Bakrah: Could you find no hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to report but this? He said: By Allah, I will report nothing to him but it until I part from him. Ziyad kept seeking permission until we were admitted. Muawiyah said: Abu Bakrah, report to us a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); perhaps Allah will benefit us by it! He said: So I reported to him again the same as my first hadith. Muawiyah said to him: May you have no father, you tell us we are kings! We are content to be kings."
"910","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, from Bahr ibn Marrar al-Bakrawi, from Abu Bakrah, who said: While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and another man was with me, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was walking between us, he came upon two graves. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two occupants of these graves are being punished now in their graves. Which of you will bring me a palm stalk from these palms? I raced my companion and beat him, broke off a palm stalk, and brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He split it in two from the top, placed half on one and half on the other, and said: It will lighten for them so long as there remains any moisture in them. They are being punished for backbiting and urine."
"911","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Jalil narrated to us: Jafar ibn Maymun narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah informed me, saying: I said to my father: Father, I hear you supplicating every morning: O Allah, grant me health in my body; O Allah, grant me health in my hearing; O Allah, grant me health in my sight; there is no god but You, repeating it three times in the evening and three times in the morning, and saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from disbelief and poverty; O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave; there is no god but You, repeating it three times in the evening and three times in the morning! He said: Yes, my son; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicating with them, so I like to follow his practice."
"912","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Jalil narrated to us: Jafar ibn Maymun narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah informed me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the supplication of the distressed: O Allah, I hope for Your mercy, so do not entrust me to myself for the blink of an eye, and set right for me all my affairs; there is no god but You."
"913","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Hashraj ibn Nubatah al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Jumhan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A group of my nation shall alight in a land called al-Basrah, where their numbers and palm trees will increase. Then the Banu Qantura, broad-faced and small-eyed, will come until they alight upon a bridge of theirs called Dijlah. The Muslims will split into three groups: one group will take hold of the tails of camels and join the desert, and perish; one group will take to themselves and disbelieve, these and those being alike; and one group will place their families behind their backs and fight; their slain are martyrs, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will grant victory to the rest of them."
"914","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, saying: I heard Abu Abdullah reporting from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, that Abu Bakrah entered upon them regarding a testimony. A man stood up from his seat for him, and Abu Bakrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man stands up for you from his seat, do not sit in it, or he said: Do not make a man stand from his seat and then sit in it, and do not wipe your hand on the garment of one you do not own. [FLAG: last clause obscure, literal]"
"915","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Fadalh narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the eclipse prayer as two rakahs."
"916","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it and break the fast upon seeing it; if it is obscured from you, complete the count as thirty days."
"917","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Fadalh narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and al-Hasan came and mounted his back, so he set him down gently. When he finished his prayer, he embraced him and kissed him. They said: Messenger of Allah, you did with al-Hasan something you did not used to do! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This son of mine is a leader; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, shall reconcile through him between two groups of Muslims."
"918","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, may Allah have mercy on him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the night prayer eight nights. Abu Bakrah said: Had you hastened this prayer, it would have been better for our standing at night! So he did."
"919","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that he reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while out of breath, and bowed before the row. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he said: Who did this? Abu Bakrah said: I did. He said: May Allah increase you in eagerness, but do not repeat."
"920","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with his Companions the fear prayer: he prayed two rakahs, then these went to the positions of those, and those came, and he prayed with them two rakahs. So for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) it was four, and for the people two and two."
"921","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jawshan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Never shall a people prosper who entrust their affair to a woman."
"922","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Uyaynah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever kills a covenanted person unduly, Allah has forbidden Paradise for him."
"923","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Uyaynah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no sin more deserving that its punishment be hastened for its doer in this world, along with what is stored for him in the Hereafter, than transgression and cutting kinship ties."
"924","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Uyaynah narrated to us, from his father, who said: The Night of Decree was mentioned before Abu Bakrah, and Abu Bakrah said: As for me, I seek it only in the last ten, after a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I heard him say: Seek it in the last ten: with nine remaining, or seven remaining, or five remaining, or three remaining, or the last night. Abu Bakrah used to pray in the first twenty of Ramadan as he prayed in the rest of the year, and when the last ten entered, he exerted himself."
"925","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jawshan narrated to us, saying: My father reported to me, saying: Nabidh used to be prepared for Abu Bakrah in an earthen jar. Abu Barzah came from an absence he had been absent, and alighted at the dwelling of Abu Bakrah before going to his own dwelling, but did not find Abu Bakrah at home. He stopped before a wife of his called Maysah, asked her about Abu Bakrah and his condition, and looked and saw the jar containing the nabidh. He said: What is in this jar? She said: Nabidh for Abu Bakrah. He said: I wish you had put it in a waterskin! Then he left. She ordered the nabidh moved into a waterskin, and hung it up. Abu Bakrah came, and she told him about Abu Barzah and his coming, then he saw the waterskin and said: What is this waterskin? She said: Abu Barzah said such-and-such, so I moved your nabidh into the waterskin. He said: I shall not drink anything of it; by Allah, were you to put honey in a jar it would be forbidden to me, and were you to put wine in a waterskin it would become lawful to me! We know what we were forbidden: we were forbidden the dubba, the naqir, the hantam, and the muzaffat. As for the dubba: we, the people of Thaqif at Taif, used to take the gourd, hollow out grape clusters into it, bury it, and leave it until it fermented and died down. As for the naqir: the people of Yamamah used to hollow out the base of the palm trunk, split ripe and unripe dates into it, and leave it until it fermented and died down. As for the hantam: jars in which wine was carried to us. As for the muzaffat: these vessels containing this pitch."
"926","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, who said: I was at the funeral of Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah. Ziyad and some of his freedmen walked on their heels before the bier, saying: Gently, gently, may Allah bless you! Abu Bakrah caught up with them in one of the lanes of al-Mirbad, charged at them on his mule and struck at them with the whip, and said: Make way; by the One who honored the face of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we saw ourselves at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) almost trotting with it at a trot."
"927","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Abu Bakrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man points a weapon at his brother, they are both on the brink of Hell; if he kills him, they both fall into it together."
"928","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Thabit Abu Zayd and Sallam narrated to us, both from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Bakrah, who said: My ears heard it from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and my heart retained it. He said: Whoever claims for other than his father, knowing he is other than his father, Paradise is forbidden to him."
"929","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Uqbah ibn Suhban, from Abu Bakrah, regarding His saying: A company of the former peoples and a company of the latter, who said: Both are of this nation. And al-Hajjaj reported this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"930","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Mihran narrated to us, from Sad ibn Aws, from Ziyad ibn Kusayb, who said: Ibn Amir went out and ascended the pulpit wearing thin garments. Abu Bilal said: Look at your commander wearing the dress of the corrupt! Abu Bakrah said from beneath the pulpit: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever dishonors the authority of Allah, Allah will dishonor him."
"931","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in the Friday prayer: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there come to you the story of the Overwhelming."
"932","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Begging is scratches with which a man scratches his face; whoever wishes may preserve his face, and whoever wishes may leave it, except that a man asks in a matter he cannot avoid, or asks one in authority. Zayd ibn Uqbah said: So I reported it to al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf, and he said: Ask me, for I am one in authority."
"933","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, from Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of what you treat yourselves with is cupping."
"934","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, saying: Firas informed me, saying: I heard al-Shabi, saying: I heard Samurah ibn Jundub say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the morning prayer and said: Is anyone here of the sons of so-and-so? Your companion is detained at the gate of Paradise by a debt upon him."
"935","Yunus narrated to us: Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah claimed, from Firas, from al-Shabi, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out twice and said: Who is here of the sons of so-and-so? No one answered him. Then in the third a man stood and said: I am. He said: What prevented you from answering me in the first two times? I mentioned your name only for good: your companion is detained at the gate of Paradise by a debt upon him. He said: So he settled it for him until none demanded anything of him."
"936","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Mujalid and Ismail, from al-Shabi, that he said: If you wish, deliver him to the punishment of Allah, and if you wish, ransom him. [FLAG: context unclear, literal]"
"937","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, who said: I heard Hilal ibn Yasaf reporting from al-Rabi ibn Umaylah, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not name your boy Aflah, nor Rabah, nor Yasar, nor Najih, lest it be said: Is he here? And it be said: No."
"938","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Masudi narrated to us, from al-Hakam and Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear these white garments, for they are purer and better, and shroud your dead in them."
"939","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, saying: al-Hakam informed me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reports from me a hadith he deems a lie is one of the liars."
"940","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, saying: Simak ibn Harb informed me, saying: I heard al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah say: I heard Samurah ibn Jundub preaching, saying in his sermon: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer before sunrise, for it rises between the two horns of Satan, or upon the two horns of a devil."
"941","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, saying: Sawadah ibn Hanzalah al-Qushayri informed me; he heard Samurah ibn Jundub preaching, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let neither the call of Bilal nor this whiteness deceive you, until the dawn bursts forth like this."
"942","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sulaym narrated to us, saying: Sawadah ibn Hanzalah al-Qushayri narrated to us, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let neither the call of Bilal prevent you from the predawn meal, nor the elongated morning, but the spreading morning on the horizon."
"943","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Hilal ibn Yasaf reporting from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If I report a hadith to you, do not add to it. Four are of the best speech, and they are of the Quran, and it will not harm you with which you begin: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great."
"944","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Hilal ibn Yasaf reporting from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not name your boy Aflah, nor Najih, nor Rabah, nor Yasar."
"945","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Qudamah ibn Wabarah, from Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever abandons Friday without excuse, let him give a dinar in charity; if he does not find, then half a dinar."
"946","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a woman and stood at her middle."
"947","Abu Dawud narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If two guardians marry off, the marriage belongs to the first of them; and if a man sells goods to two men, it belongs to the first of them."
"948","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of the house has more right to the house."
"949","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we kill him; whoever cuts him, we cut him; whoever castrates him, we castrate him."
"950","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever encloses a wall around land, it is his."
"951","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a caller, who called out on a rainy day: The prayer is in the dwellings."
"952","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah or Uqbah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The liability for defect of a slave is four days."
"953","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every boy is pledged for his aqiqah."
"954","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever owns a relative of unmarriageable kin is free."
"955","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse with the curse of Allah, nor with the anger of Allah, nor with the Fire."
"956","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man shall not outbid his brother, nor propose over his proposal."
"957","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Fadalh narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn al-Mughaffal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to pray in sheep pens, and not to pray in camel resting places, for they were created of devils."
"958","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who heard Uqbah ibn Suhban, from Abdullah ibn al-Mughaffal al-Muzani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade khadhf and said: It neither catches game nor harms an enemy; khadhf breaks the tooth and gouges the eye."
"959","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Abdullah ibn al-Mughaffal, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Surah al-Fath on the day of the Conquest, repeating the melody. Were people not to gather about me, I would have sung it for you in that voice."
"960","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Wasil narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Abdullah ibn al-Mughaffal al-Muzani, who said: The first I saw wearing leather socks in Islam was al-Mughirah ibn Shubah; he came to us while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing two black socks. We looked at them and marveled at them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They shall have plenty of socks; they said: Messenger of Allah, what shall we do? He said: Wipe over them and pray."
"961","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah and Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah al-Qaysi narrated to us, both from Humayd ibn Hilal al-Adawi, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Mughaffal, may Allah have mercy on him, say: A bag of fat was let down on the day of Khaybar. I took it and clasped it, and said: This is mine; I shall give none of it to anyone! I turned, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I felt ashamed before him. Sulayman said in his hadith, and it is not in the hadith of Shubah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is yours. Abu Dawud said: As if from the spoils."
"962","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Thabit ibn Yazid Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Fudayl al-Raqashi, who said: I asked Abdullah ibn al-Mughaffal, saying: What of this drink is forbidden to us? He said: Wine. He said: I said: Is this in the Quran? He said: I only report to you what I heard from Muhammad the Messenger, or the Messenger Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whether he began with the messengership or the name. He said: I said: Enough for me, meaning he said: He forbade the hantam. He said: I said: What is the hantam? He said: The green and white jar, and the naqir and the muzaffat. He said: I said: What is the muzaffat? He said: What has tar put in it, of vessel or otherwise. And the dubba. He said: So I bought a small waterskin, prepared nabidh in it, and hung it up. Abu Dawud said: An ufayqah is like a waterskin."
"963","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Mughaffal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade khadhf."
"964","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Sayyar ibn Salamah Abu al-Minhal, that he heard Abu Barzah, and my father asked him: How was your prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He used to pray with us the midday, which you call Zuhr, when the sun had declined; pray with us Asr while the sun was alive, and I forgot what he said about Maghrib; he used to pray with us Isha, not minding to delay it to a third of the night; he disliked sleep before it and talk after it; and he used to pray with us Fajr, and one of us would leave knowing his neighbor; and he used to recite in it from sixty to a hundred."
"965","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, Hammad said: And Sayyar ibn Salamah reported to me, from Abu Barzah. One of them said: Bilal used to call when the sun declined, and the other said: When the sun had passed its zenith. [FLAG: two wordings, literal]"
"966","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Jamil ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Wadi al-Sahtani, who said: We went out on a raid of ours and alighted at a stop. A man bought a slave for a horse. We remained the rest of our day and night. When it was time to depart, the man stood to his horse to saddle it, and the man held him to the sale. They disputed to Abu Barzah al-Aslami, who said: Are you both content that I judge between you by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that the two traders retain the option so long as they have not parted. Hammad said: This is what I retained. Hammad said: Hisham ibn Hassan said in this chain: Abu Barzah said: And I do not see you two have parted."
"967","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Sharik ibn Shihab, who said: I used to wish to meet a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to ask him about the Kharijites. I met Abu Barzah al-Aslami on a feast day among some of his companions, and said to him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speak about the Kharijites? Abu Barzah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my ears and saw him with my eyes. Wealth was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he divided it. A black man with cropped hair, wearing two white garments, came; he gave those on his right and those on his left and gave him nothing. He came from behind him and said: By Allah, Muhammad, you have not been just! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, you will find none after me more just to you than me, saying it three times. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A people shall emerge at the end of time, as if this one is of them; they recite the Quran, but it does not pass their throats; they pass out of Islam as the arrow passes out of the target; their mark is shaving; they shall keep emerging until the last of them emerges with the Antichrist. When you meet them, kill them; they are the worst of creation."
"968","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Kinanah ibn Nuaym al-Adawi, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on one of his expeditions. When he finished fighting, he said: Do you miss anyone? They said: By Allah, we miss so-and-so and so-and-so. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look, do you miss anyone? They said: We miss so-and-so and so-and-so. He said: But I miss Julaybib; seek him. They found him beside seven he had killed and who then killed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought and told. He came to him and said: He killed seven, then they killed him! He is of me and I am of him; he killed seven and they killed him! He is of me and I am of him, saying it twice or thrice. Then he said with his forearms like this, and spread them; he was placed upon the forearms of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until a grave was dug for him. He had no bed but the forearms of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he was buried. He said: And he mentioned no washing."
"969","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Barzah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah forgive Ghifar, and may Allah grant peace to Aslam."
"970","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Sayyar ibn Salamah, from Abu Barzah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The leaders are of Quraysh, so long as they act by three. [FLAG: wording truncated in print, literal]"
"971","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, who said: I was sitting on a cliff at al-Ahwaz when an old man praying came, having fastened his mount's bridle in his hand. The beast stepped back, and he stepped back with it. A man of the Kharijites with us began reviling him. When he finished his prayer, he said: I heard your talk. I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) such-and-such raid, witnessed his command and his facilitation, and holding my beast is easier for me than letting it go to its stable and troubling me. He said: And there was Abu Barzah al-Aslami."
"972","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn Abi Layla Abu al-Mualla al-Adawi narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Hasan say: Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad entered upon Maqil ibn Yasar, and Maqil ibn Yasar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever enters into anything of the prices of the Muslims to raise it against them, it is due upon Allah to cast him into the mightiest part of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"973","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Fadalh, Abbad ibn Rashid, and Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad entered upon Maqil ibn Yasar, and said: Report to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); perhaps Allah will benefit me! He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is put in charge of subjects and dies while deceiving them, Allah has forbidden Paradise for him."
"974","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abbad ibn Rashid and al-Mubarak ibn Fadalh narrated to us, from al-Hasan, Abbad said: I heard al-Hasan say: Maqil ibn Yasar al-Muzani reported to me, saying: I had a sister who was sought of me in marriage, and I kept men from her, until a cousin of mine came and sought her of me, so I married her to him. They lived together as long as Allah willed, then he divorced her a divorce in which he had return, then left her until her waiting period ended. Then he came seeking her with the suitors. I said: You wretch, my sister was sought of me and I kept men from her; you sought her of me, so I favored you with her and married her to you, then you divorced her. Then you did not seek her until her waiting period ended. When the suitors came seeking her, you came seeking her! No, by Allah, besides whom there is no god, I shall never marry her to you. Maqil said: Concerning me this verse was revealed: And when you divorce women and they reach their term, do not prevent them from marrying their husbands when they agree among themselves in kindness. He said: And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, knew her need of him and his need of her, so this verse was revealed. I said: Hearing and obeying! So I married her to him and expiated my oath."
"975","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from a man, from his father, from Maqil ibn Yasar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite Ya Sin over your dead."
"976","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mualla al-Qardusi, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Maqil ibn Yasar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Worship in turmoil is like emigration to me."
"977","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mualla al-Qardusi, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Maqil ibn Yasar, that two men disputed to him over land. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever swears an oath to cut off thereby the wealth of his brother shall meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him."
"978","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Muthanna ibn Awf narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydullah, from Maqil, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fadikh. Thus in the Hijr edition, with the editor noting the manuscripts so read and that the correct is Abu Abdullah. [FLAG: editor note, literal]"
"979","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah reported to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, who heard Jundub say: Gabriel tarried from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so a woman said: I see his companion has but tarried from him! So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: By the morning light, and the night when it covers, your Lord has not forsaken you nor does He hate you."
"980","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Aswad, who heard Jundub say: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching on the day of sacrifice. He said: Whoever of you slaughtered before the prayer, let him repeat another in place of his sacrifice; and whoever has not slaughtered, let him slaughter in the name of Allah."
"981","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Aswad, who heard Jundub say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to prayer and his toe stumbled and bled. He said: You are but a toe that bled; what befell you was in the path of Allah. [FLAG: print text truncated; completed from sense]"
"982","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, who heard Jundub al-Bajali say: Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; whoever violates Allah in His protection, Allah will throw him on his face into the Fire. And Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal reported this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"983","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lodged them in a dome in the mosque to soften their hearts. When they accepted Islam, they stipulated upon him that they not be gathered for war, nor tithed, nor taxed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You shall not be gathered, nor tithed, nor taxed, and there is no good in a religion in which there is no bowing. Abu Dawud said: Ibn Fadalh said: I heard al-Hasan add in this hadith that Thaqif said: We shall give it to you despite dislike in it. [FLAG: obscure clause, literal]"
"984","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, saying: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyib, saying: Uthman ibn Abi al-As reported, saying: The last the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me, he said: When you lead people, lighten the prayer for them."
"985","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah al-Madani, from Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik al-Ansari, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you complains, let him place his hand where he feels pain, then say: I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power over all things from the evil of what I feel, saying that seven times. And Malik ibn Anas reports this hadith from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"986","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and the Gatherer, and the Prophet of Repentance, and the Prophet of Battle."
"987","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, saying: One of my brothers reported to me, from my father, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, who said: I came to Madinah for the ransom of Badr, and he was then a polytheist. He said: I entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying Maghrib, reciting at-Tur in it, and my heart was as if rent by the recitation of the Quran."
"988","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, Abu Dawud said: I know it only from his father, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about something she mentioned to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Return to me. She said: Messenger of Allah, what if I come and do not find you, to whom then? He said: To Abu Bakr. And this hadith was reported from Sad ibn Ibrahim without doubt."
"989","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from his maternal uncle al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a road between Makkah and Madinah. He said: The people of Yemen are about to appear before you as if pieces of cloud, or a piece of cloud; they are the best of those on earth. A man of the Ansar said: And not we, Messenger of Allah? He was silent. Then he said: And not we, Messenger of Allah? He was silent. Then he said: And not we, Messenger of Allah? He was silent. Then he said: Except you, in a faint utterance. [FLAG: obscure adverb, literal]"
"990","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite at-Tur in Maghrib."
"991","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Murrah informed me; he heard Asim al-Anazi reporting from Ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered prayer, said the takbir. He said: Allah is Most Great, greatly, saying it three times; praise be to Allah abundantly, saying it three times; glory be to Allah morning and evening, saying it three times; I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan, from his puffing, spitting, and prodding."
"992","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Sulayman ibn Surad, who said: I heard Jubayr ibn Mutim say: Washing from major impurity was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for me, I pour over my head three times."
"993","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from an-Numan ibn Salim, from a man, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, who said: I said: Messenger of Allah, your Companions claim we have no rewards for our stay in Makkah! He said: Your rewards shall surely come to you even were in a burrow. He said: He inclined his head to me and said: Among my Companions are hypocrites."
"994","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Rukanah, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers, or he said: a hundred, elsewhere, except al-Masjid al-Haram. [FLAG: doubt in number, literal]"
"995","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Azhar, from Jubayr ibn Mutim, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Qurashi has twice the strength of two men of others. It was said to az-Zuhri: Why is that? He said: By soundness of judgment."
"996","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zamah narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the slave girl of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her; if she repeats, let him flog her; if she repeats, let him flog her; if she repeats a fourth time, let him sell her even for a braid of hair."
"997","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zamah narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Zayd ibn Khalid, who said: Two disputants came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Messenger of Allah, we adjure you by Allah but that you judge between us by the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic! His opponent, more understanding than he, stood and said: Yes, Messenger of Allah; judge between us by the Book of Allah and permit me to speak! He permitted him. He said: Messenger of Allah, my son was a laborer for this one, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told my son deserved stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a servant. When I asked the people of knowledge, they told me my son deserved a hundred lashes and a year's banishment, and this man's wife deserved stoning! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I shall surely judge between you by the Book of Allah: the hundred sheep and servant are returned to you; your son deserves a hundred lashes and a year's banishment; go, Unays, to this man's wife, and if she confesses, stone her. So he went to her in the morning, asked her, and she confessed, and he stoned her."
"998","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Salih, freedman of at-Tawamah, from Zayd ibn Khalid, who said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then come to the market; if we shot arrows, we could see their landing places."
"999","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Zayd ibn Khalid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever perfects ablution then prays two rakahs without heedlessness in them is forgiven. And Abu Amir reports this hadith from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Khalid."
"1000","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a fighter in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has fought; and whoever looks after him in his family with good has fought."
"1001","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Zayd ibn Khalid, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the rooster, for it calls to prayer. And Abu Dawud said another time: From Abd al-Aziz, from Salih, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, and this is more established in my view."
"1002","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi ibn Habban, who heard Rafi ibn Khadij; he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no cutting for fruit or palm pith."
"1003","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Rafi ibn Khadij, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray the morning prayer at dawn brightness, for it is greater in reward."
"1004","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ata, from Rafi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sows in the land of people without their permission has nothing of the crop, but his expenses."
"1005","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurayr ibn Rafi ibn Khadij, from Rafi ibn Khadij, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Bilal: Pray the morning prayer at brightness, until the people can see the landing places of their arrows."
"1006","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Ansari reported to me, saying: My grandfather reported to me, from Rafi ibn Khadij, that an arrow struck him with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in one of his raids. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Rafi, if you wish, I shall pull out the arrow and leave the head, and I shall bear witness for you on the Day of Resurrection that you are a martyr. So he did. [FLAG: manuscript variant noted in print, literal]"
"1007","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zaidah ibn Qudamah ath-Thaqafi narrated to us, Abu Dawud said: He would not report to a Qadari nor a known innovator; he said: Said ibn Masruq ath-Thawri narrated to us, from Abayah ibn Rifah ibn Rafi ibn Khadij, from his grandfather Rafi, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Dhu al-Hulayfah of Tihamah, and the people hungered and seized camels and sheep. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them with the pots set up; he commanded regarding the pots and they were overturned, then he divided among them, equating ten sheep to a camel. He said: A camel of the people's camels fled, and there were but few horses among the people; a man shot it with an arrow and stopped it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These camels have wildness like the wildness of game; what overcomes you of them, do thus with it."
"1008","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zaidah narrated to us, from Said ibn Masruq, from Abayah, from Rafi, who said: We said: Messenger of Allah, we shall meet the enemy tomorrow and have no knives; shall we slaughter with reeds? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What causes blood to flow and Allah's name is mentioned over it, eat; except tooth and nail. I shall tell you about that: as for tooth, it is bone; as for nail, it is the knives of the Abyssinians. Abu Dawud said: Zaidah said: Do you see any hadith in the world on this chapter better than it? Abu Dawud said: By Allah, it is among the finest hadith."
"1009","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: We saw no harm in sharecropping until Ibn Khadij claimed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"1010","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Rafi ibn Khadij, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade haql. Shubah said: I said to al-Hakam: What is haql? He said: A third and a quarter. Shubah said: Al-Hakam said: When Ibrahim heard this hadith, he disliked a third and a quarter, but saw no harm in renting land for gold and silver."
"1011","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz, from as-Saib ibn Yazid, from Rafi ibn Khadij, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earnings of the cupper are foul, the dower of the adulteress is foul, and the price of the dog is foul."
"1012","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, who heard Abu al-Bakhtari reporting from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: When this verse, When the help of Allah comes and the victory, was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it to its end, then said: I and my Companions are one side and people are another side; no emigration after the Conquest. Abu Said said: So I reported this hadith to Marwan ibn al-Hakam, who was governor of Madinah, and he said: You have lied, while Rafi ibn Khadij was with him. I said: This one, if he wished, could report to you. Rafi said: He spoke the truth."
"1013","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Mujahid, from Rafi ibn Khadij, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has land, let him grant it to his brother and not rent it out. And Sufyan reported this hadith from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Usayd ibn Zuhayr, from Rafi ibn Khadij."
"1014","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, saying: Abu Balj Yahya ibn Sulaym informed me, saying: I heard Abayah ibn Rifah ibn Rafi ibn Khadij reporting that his grandfather died leaving a cupper boy, a water camel, land, and a slave girl. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that the cupper's earnings be put into the fodder of the water camel, forbade the slave girl's earnings, and said regarding the land: Cultivate it or leave it."
"1015","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ath-Thawri narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, from his father, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) call the adhan in the ear of al-Hasan when his mother Fatimah bore him, with the prayer."
"1016","1014 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a young camel from a man, then the man came demanding repayment, so he ordered Abu Rafi' to repay him, and he said: I find nothing but a choice camel! He said: ""Give it to him, for the best of you — or he said: the best of people — are those best in repayment."" And al-Qa'nabi narrated this hadith from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Rafi', from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1017","1015 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Rafi', from Abu Rafi', that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man from Banu Makhzum over the charity, and he said to Abu Rafi': Accompany me so that you may get some of it! He said: No, until I go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him! So he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, and he said: Charity is not lawful for us, and the freedman of a people is from among themselves."
"1018","1016 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'la al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The neighbor has more right to what adjoins his land."" And Sufyan narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, from Abu Rafi', from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1019","1017 - Abu Dawud narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Ibn Abi Rafi', that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed the short spear to Abu Rafi' and ordered him to kill the dogs of Madinah, so he killed them except one dog, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he ordered him to kill it. And al-Qa'nabi narrated this hadith from Ya'qub ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd ibn Zurarah, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abu Rafi'."
"1020","1018 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Mukhawwal, from Abu Sa'id, from Abu Rafi', who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was prostrating with my hair tied up in a knot, so he undid it."
"1021","1019 - Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Tammam, from his grandfather al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade branding on the face. Al-Abbas said: I brand only on the farthest bone, so he branded at the far end of the buttocks."
"1022","1020 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Abu al-Aliyah, that al-Abbas built an upper chamber, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Demolish it. He said: Should I rather give its price in charity? He said: ""Demolish it,"" three times."
"1023","1021 - Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abu Isra'il narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever intends Hajj should hasten to it, for the sick person falls ill, the stray mount strays, and need arises."" Abu Dawud expressed doubt in this hadith, while others narrated it without doubt from Abu Isra'il, from Fudayl, from Abu Sa'id, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl."
"1024","1022 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued reciting the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"1025","1023 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman from Khath'am came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Farewell Hajj and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation of Hajj upon His servants has reached my father as a very old man unable to hold himself firmly on the mount; would it suffice for him if I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: ""Yes."" Thus Abu Dawud narrated it, while Abd al-Razzaq said: from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1026","1024 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas, that he rode behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his mount did not lift a foreleg going in the morning until he stoned the Jamarah."
"1027","1025 - Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating cucumber with fresh dates."
"1028","1026 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ja'far, from his father, that when the news of Ja'far's death came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Prepare food for the family of Ja'far, for there has come to them what occupies them."" Thus Abu Dawud said, while others said: from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Khalid ibn Ja'far, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far."
"1029","1027 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Muwarriq, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would return from a journey, I and al-Hasan would be brought out to meet him, and he would place one of us in front of him and the other behind him on the mount."
"1030","1028 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, he said: One who witnessed Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed me, while Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr was cutting meat for Abdullah ibn Ja'far and feeding him, that Ibn Ja'far said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The best meat is the back."""
"1031","1029 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'qub, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, who said: When the news of the killing of Ja'far and his companions reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he gave the family of Ja'far three days' respite, then he came to them and said: ""Bring out to me the sons of my brother."" So three were brought out as if they were chicks: Abdullah, Awn, and Muhammad. He called the barber and he shaved their heads, and said: ""As for Awn, he resembles me in appearance and character, and as for Muhammad, he resembles our uncle Abu Talib."" He took Abdullah by the hand and raised it and said: ""O Allah, succeed Ja'far in his family, and bless Abdullah in the deal of his right hand."" He said: Their mother began to express joy for them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do you fear poverty for them while I am their guardian in this world and the Hereafter?"" Thus Abu Dawud narrated it, while Wahb ibn Jarir narrated it from his father, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, who said: Our mother brought us to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1032","1030 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Jabir, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped on his neck after he had been poisoned."
"1033","1031 - Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The soul of the believer is a bird that clings to the trees of Paradise until Allah, Almighty and Majestic, returns it to its body."" And Abd al-Razzaq narrates this hadith from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father."
"1034","1032 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his uncle, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing women and children."
"1035","1033 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, who said: I heard Ka'b say: ""When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on an expedition, he would allude to something else."""
"1036","1034 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik — who was Ka'b's guide when he became blind — he said: I heard Ka'b narrating his report when he stayed behind from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk. Ka'b said: I never stayed behind from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in any expedition he ever fought except in the expedition of Tabuk, though I had not witnessed Badr, and Allah did not blame anyone who stayed behind from Badr; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had only gone out seeking the caravan of Quraysh until Allah, Almighty and Majestic, brought him together with his enemy without an appointment. And I had witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the night of al-Aqabah when we pledged one another upon Islam, and I would not wish to have in its place the witnessing of Badr, though Badr is more remembered among the people than it. Part of my story is that when I stayed behind from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk, I had never been stronger or wealthier than when I stayed behind from him; by Allah, two mounts had never been gathered for me until I gathered them in that expedition. Ka'b said: Anyone who intended to stay behind from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I would assume it would remain hidden for him unless Allah, Almighty and Majestic, sent down revelation concerning him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on campaign when the fruits of Madinah had ripened and its shade was pleasant, and I was inclined toward them, yet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced the direction he intended, though when he went on an expedition he would allude to something else, until that expedition came; and the people with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were many, whom no preserving register could encompass — meaning the diwan. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced a distant journey, and we were a large number, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to prepare, and I would go out in the morning as if preparing, then return having accomplished nothing; then I would go out in the morning as if preparing and accomplish nothing. He said: The matter kept dragging on with me until the people hastened to depart, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in the morning with the Muslims with him, so I intended to set out but it was not decreed for me — would that I had done so! It grieved me that when I went out after the departure of the Messenger of Allah among the people, I saw none but a man accused of hypocrisy or a man among the weak whom Allah had excused. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not mention me until he reached Tabuk, where he said in an assembly — with Mu'adh ibn Jabal among the people — at Tabuk: ""What did Ka'b ibn Malik do?"" A man from Banu Salimah said: His two cloaks and his looking at his sides have detained him, O Messenger of Allah! Mu'adh said: Evil, by Allah, is what you have said; by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I know nothing but good! While the Messenger of Allah was thus, he saw a man obscured by the mirage, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Be Abu Khaythamah."" And it was Abu Khaythamah, who had given charity of a sa' and the hypocrites had mocked him, for he found nothing but his own effort. When it reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had turned back from Tabuk, my anguish and lying came upon me, and I began to say: How shall I escape the anger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I sought help for that from every sensible person among my family. When it reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was about to arrive, falsehood departed from me and I resolved upon his truthfulness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he returned from a journey, would begin with the mosque and pray two rak'ahs in it; when he did that, the hypocrites — eighty-four men — would come to him, offering excuses and swearing to him, and he would accept their outward conduct, seek forgiveness for them, and leave their secrets to Allah. Then I came, and when he saw me he smiled the smile of one angry, then said: ""What kept you behind? Had you not purchased your mount?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, had I been with anyone else among the people of this world, I would have thought I could escape his anger, for I have been given skill in argument; but by Allah, if I narrate to you today a report with which you are pleased with me, Allah will soon make you angry with me, and if I narrate to you today a truthful report at which you are angry with me, I hope for Allah's good outcome. No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I had never been stronger or wealthier than when I stayed behind from you; by Allah, two mounts had never been gathered for me until I gathered them in this expedition! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""As for this one, he has told me the truth; stand until Allah decides concerning you."" He said: So I stood, and men of my people from Banu Salimah turned to me and said: By Allah, we never knew you to have committed a sin in Islam before this; the seeking of forgiveness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have sufficed for your sin — would you not have offered the Messenger of Allah the excuse the stragglers offered him? He said: By Allah, they kept blaming me until I almost belied myself. He said: So I said: Has anyone else met what I met? He said: Two men met with you what was said to you. I said: Who are they? They said: Hilal ibn Umayyah al-Waqifi and Murarah ibn al-Rabi' al-Amiri — they mentioned two righteous men who had witnessed Badr, in whom there is an example for me. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade speaking to us, we three men, apart from those who stayed behind from him. He said: The people avoided us and would not speak to us, so by Allah I myself became unfamiliar to me, and the earth became unfamiliar to me in myself, so it was not the earth I had known. As for my two companions, they submitted and sat in their houses, while I was the youngest of the people and the strongest, so I would attend the prayer with the Muslims and wander in the markets with none speaking to me. I would come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pray with him, then greet him and say to myself: Did he move his lips in reply to me? I would steal glances at him: when I turned to my prayer he turned toward me, and when I turned toward him he turned away from me. When that estrangement of the Muslims from us grew long for me, I went to Abu Qatadah — my cousin and the most beloved of people to me — and spoke to him, but by Allah he did not speak to me. I said: O Abu Qatadah, I adjure you by Allah, do you know that I love Allah and His Messenger? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: My eyes overflowed, so I climbed over the wall and went away. While I was in the market one day, a Nabataean from the Nabataeans of Syria came to me with a letter from the king of Ghassan, saying: Who will guide me to Ka'b ibn Malik? The people began pointing to me. I took the letter — and I was literate, I could read — and it was from the king of Ghassan, and in it: To proceed: It has reached us that your companion has banished you, and Allah has not placed you in an abode of humiliation or loss, so join us and we shall console you! He said: I said: This too is part of the evil. I took the letter and headed with it to the oven and burned it. When forty nights had passed since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade speaking to us, the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and said: The Messenger of Allah commands you to keep away from your wife. I said: Shall I divorce her, or what shall I do with her? He said: Do not approach her. So I said to my wife: Go to your family until Allah decides in this matter — and he sent the like of that to my two companions. He said: The wife of Hilal ibn Umayyah came and said: O Messenger of Allah, Hilal is a wasted man with no servant; would you dislike that I serve him? He said: ""No, but let him not approach you."" She said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah there has been no movement from him toward any of that since what happened happened; he only weeps. One of my family said to me: Why do you not seek permission from the Messenger of Allah concerning your wife, when he has permitted the wife of Hilal? I said: By Allah, I shall not do so, for I am a young man and do not know what the Messenger of Allah will say. He said: While I was thus, on the morning of the fiftieth night since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade speaking to us, I prayed the dawn prayer on the roof of a house of ours, then sat in the state Allah described: {The earth became straitened for them despite its vastness, and their selves became straitened for them, and they thought there is no refuge from Allah except to Him}. Then I heard the voice of a crier who had ascended Sal', and a man galloped to me on a horse, and the voice was quicker to me than the horse: Glad tidings, O Ka'b ibn Malik! I fell down prostrate and knew that relief had come. The one whose voice I had heard came to me, so I stripped off the two garments I wore — by Allah I owned nothing besides them — and clothed him with them as glad tidings, then borrowed two garments and wore them, then set out heading for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ka'b said: Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — who was kind concerning my affair — informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with her that night, and when a third of the night remained, our repentance was sent down upon him, and he said to her: ""O Umm Salamah, Ka'b ibn Malik and his two companions have been forgiven."" She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not send to him and give him glad tidings? He said: ""Then the people would crowd you and deprive you of sleep the rest of the night."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced Allah's turning in forgiveness toward us after he prayed the dawn prayer. He said: Announcers went toward my two companions, and announcers went toward me. Ka'b said: So I set out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the Muhajirun and Ansar around him; his face had lit up as if it were a piece of the moon — and when he was pleased with something his face would light up. Talhah ibn Ubaydillah, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up for me, hurrying until he congratulated me and shook my hand; by Allah no man of the Muhajirun stood besides him, and Ka'b would never forget it for Talhah. He said: The Muslims began congratulating me for Allah's turning toward me, saying: May Allah's turning toward you please you, may Allah's turning toward you please you, until I reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he saw me he said: ""Come, O Ka'b, and receive glad tidings of the best day that has come upon you since the day your mother bore you."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, is it from you or from Allah? He said: ""Rather, from Allah."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, part of my repentance is to divest myself of all my wealth as charity to Allah and to His Messenger. He said: ""O Ka'b, keep some of your wealth, for it is better for you."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shall keep my share which is at Khaybar. And I said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah, Almighty and Majestic, saved me only through truthfulness, and part of my repentance is never to speak but the truth as long as I live. Ka'b said: By Allah, I know no one whom Allah has tested in truthfulness of speech like that with which He tested me; by Allah, I have never deliberately lied since I said that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until this day of mine, and I hope Allah will protect me in what remains. He said: Then Allah, Almighty and Majestic, sent down: {Allah has turned in forgiveness to the Prophet and the Muhajirun and the Ansar} — both verses together."
"1037","1035 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Humaydah bint Abi Ubaydah al-Ansariyyah, from her mother, from Ka'b ibn Malik al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said upon the pulpit: I came out intending to inform you of Laylat al-Qadr but I was made to forget it, so seek it in the last ten nights, in the odd nights."
"1038","1036 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to travel on Thursdays."
"1039","1037 - Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa', from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever draws the sword against us is not of us."""
"1040","1038 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ya'la ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Iyas ibn Salamah narrated to us, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead us in the Friday prayer, and we would leave with the walls having no shade in which to seek shade."
"1041","1039 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, from Iyas ibn Salamah, from his father, who said: We went on an expedition with Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, against Hawazin. I outran the people to the mountain and drove back a group of people, and I captured a woman from Fazarah who had a daughter among the most beautiful of the Arabs, so Abu Bakr gave me the daughter of the Fazari woman as an extra share. When we arrived, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""O Salamah, give me the woman, may your father be sacrificed for Allah!"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have not uncovered her! He said: ""Give her to me, may your father be sacrificed for Allah!"" I said: She is yours, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So he sent her to the people of Makkah and ransomed with her a captive who was in their hands."
"1042","1040 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Umar ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ghifar — may Allah forgive them — and Aslam — may Allah, Almighty and Majestic, grant them peace."""
"1043","1041 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of our foot soldiers is Salamah, and the best of our horsemen is Abu Qatadah."""
"1044","1042 - Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, that a man peeked into the room of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had an iron comb with which he was scratching his head, so he said: Had I known you were looking, I would have stood to stab you in your eyes with it; permission was only instituted because of sight."
"1045","1043 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Kharijah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Abu Hazim al-Madani, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We used to rejoice at Friday, and that is because we would visit an old woman who would prepare beetroot and barley for us, and we would eat it and then return in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1046","1044 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: Most of those who prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were the companions of knots. He said: I said: What are the companions of knots? He said: None of them had but a single garment, which he would tie upon his neck."
"1047","1045 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away leaving a woolen cloak still at the weaver's."
"1048","1046 - Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Jarir ibn Abdullah, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away at sixty-three, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, at sixty-three, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, at sixty-three."
"1049","1047 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, who said: I heard Ma'bad al-Juhani say: Mu'awiyah rarely narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but he had some speech on Fridays which he would narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Whomever Allah wills good for, He gives him understanding in the religion; and this wealth is sweet and green — whoever takes it rightfully is blessed in it for him. And beware of excessive mutual praise, for mutual praise is slaughter."
"1050","1048 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Mu'awiyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The life-grant is permissible for its people."""
"1051","1049 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from al-Hakam ibn Mina, from Ibn Jariyah, who said: We were at the door of Mu'awiyah, and he came out to us and said: What were you discussing? We said: We were discussing the Ansar and their reports. Mu'awiyah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him, and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him."""
"1052","1050 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Tayyah informed me, from Ma'bad al-Juhani, who said: Mu'awiyah addressed us and said: What is with people who pray a prayer — I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and never saw him pray it, and we heard him forbidding it — meaning the two rak'ahs after Asr."
"1053","1051 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Isa ibn Talhah, who said: I heard Mu'awiyah say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Talhah is among those who fulfilled their vow."""
"1054","1052 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Isa ibn Talhah, who said: We were with Mu'awiyah when the caller called to prayer, and he said the like of what he said, then said: Thus I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1055","1053 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah and Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Abu Mijlaz, who said: Mu'awiyah came out, and Ibn Amir stood up for him while Ibn al-Zubayr remained seated, and he was the more balanced of the two. Mu'awiyah said to Ibn Amir: Sit, for I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever loves that men stand up for him, let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"1056","1054 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Mu'awiyah, who said: ""Laylat al-Qadr is the night of the twenty-seventh."" Thus Abu Dawud said, and it has reached me that Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh raised it."
"1057","1055 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Shaykh al-Huna'i, that Mu'awiyah said to a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade leopard-skin saddle cloths? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And I bear witness. He said: Do you know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing gold except in small pieces? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: Do you know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade joining Hajj and Umrah? They said: O Allah, no. He said: By Allah, it is indeed among them."
"1058","1056 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib say: Mu'awiyah came to Madinah and addressed us, and he brought out a ball of hair and said: I did not think anyone did this but the Jews; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called it falsehood."
"1059","1057 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id, who said: Mu'awiyah addressed us and said: You have innovated an evil adornment; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade falsehood. Qatadah said: It is what women place on their heads of rags."
"1060","1058 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Yazid ibn Tahman al-Raqashi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, who said: Mu'awiyah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Do not ride silk-wool garments nor leopard skins."" Muhammad said: When Mu'awiyah narrated the like of this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he was not suspected. And Abu Dawud said another time: When Mu'awiyah narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he was not suspected."
"1061","1059 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Jarad informed me, he said: I heard Raja ibn Haywah narrating from Mu'awiyah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whomever Allah wills good for, He gives him understanding in the religion."""
"1062","1060 - Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ulayy, from his father, from Amr ibn al-As, who said: There was a panic in Madinah, and the people began going this way and that, so I entered the mosque and there was Salim, freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, sitting wrapped in his sword straps at the pulpit — the pulpit of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I sat with Salim, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and ascended the pulpit and said: ""O people, was not your refuge to Allah and His Messenger? Would you not do as these two believing men did?"""
"1063","1061 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ulayy, from his father, who said: I heard Amr ibn al-As say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to me: ""Put on your weapons and come to me."" So I did, and I entered upon him, and he lowered his gaze at me and raised it, and said to me: ""O Amr, I intend to send you on an expedition, through which Allah will grant you booty, and I shall apportion for you a generous share of wealth."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I did not embrace Islam for wealth! He said: ""O Amr, excellent indeed is righteous wealth for a righteous man."""
"1064","1062 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, who said: Amr ibn al-As said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the most beloved of people to you? He said: ""Aishah."" He said: I mean among men. He said: ""Her father."" He said: And this hadith is narrated from Khalid, from Abu Uthman, from Amr ibn al-As."
"1065","1063 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from a man of the people of Egypt, who said: I witnessed Amr ibn al-As when Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr was brought to him — and he was the governor over Egypt — bound, and Amr said to him: Do you have a pledge of safety? Has anyone granted you safety? He did not mention that he had any pledge. Amr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The lowest of the Muslims grants protection on their behalf."" He said: So his neck was struck."
"1066","1064 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab narrated to us, who said: Amr ibn al-As was in severe anguish at death, so his son Abdullah said to him: What is this anguish, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to employ you and draw you near? He said: O my son, I shall inform you of that. He said: He used to do that, but by Allah I do not know whether it was out of love or conciliating me. But I bear witness concerning two men whom he left this world loving them: Ibn Umm Abd and Ibn Sumayyah."
"1067","1065 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, who said: I heard Dhakwan narrating from a freedman of Amr ibn al-As that he sent him to Ali seeking permission regarding Asma bint Umays, and he gave him permission. When he had finished his need, the freedman asked Amr about that, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us — or he forbade — entering upon women without the permission of their husbands."
"1068","1066 - Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, who heard Alqamah, who said: I arrived in Syria and entered the mosque and said: O Allah, grant me a righteous companion to sit with. He said: So I sat with a man, and he was Abu al-Darda. He said to me: From where are you? I said: From the people of Kufah. He said: Is there not among you the companion of the pillow and the siwak? — meaning Ibn Mas'ud. Then he said: Is there not among you the keeper of the secret which none knew but him? — meaning Hudhayfah. Then he said: Is there not among you the one whom Allah protected from Satan upon the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? — meaning Ammar. Then he said: Do you know how Abdullah used to recite {By the night when it covers} — and the male and the female? I said: He used to recite it {By the night when it covers, by the day when it appears}. Abu al-Darda said: By Allah, these kept at me until they almost made me doubt. Abu al-Darda said: Thus we recite it, and thus I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting it."
"1069","1067 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrating from Ma'dan ibn Abi Talhah, from Abu al-Darda, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Is any of you unable to recite a third of the Quran in a night?"" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who can bear that? He said: ""Read {Say: He is Allah, the One}."""
"1070","1068 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from a nephew of Adi ibn Artah, from a man, from Abu al-Darda, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What I fear most for you are the misleading imams."""
"1071","1069 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Abu Salih narrating from Ata ibn Yasar, from a man, from Abu al-Darda, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about His saying: {Those who believed and were God-fearing — for them are glad tidings in the life of this world}. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is the righteous dream which the Muslim sees or which is seen for him."""
"1072","1070 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr narrating from his father, from Abu al-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a visibly pregnant woman at the door of a tent — or he said: a small tent — and said: ""Perhaps the owner of this one approaches her! I intended to curse him with a curse that would enter the grave with him. How can he bequeath to him when it is not lawful for him? And how can he enslave him when it is not lawful for him?"""
"1073","1071 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah informed me, he said: I heard Ata narrating from Umm al-Darda, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — or from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Nothing heavier than good character is placed in the scale on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1074","1072 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Khulayd al-Asri, from Abu al-Darda, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No sun has ever risen but Allah, Almighty and Majestic, sends at its two sides two angels calling out, making all creation hear except the two weighty beings: O Allah, hasten a replacement for the spender, and give the withholder loss. And no sun has ever set but Allah, Almighty and Majestic, sends at its two sides two angels calling out, making creation hear except the two weighty beings: Little that suffices is better than much that distracts."""
"1075","1073 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Habibah al-Ta'i, from Abu al-Darda, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The likeness of one who gives charity or frees a slave at death is like one who gives a gift after he is satiated."""
"1076","1074 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abu al-Darda, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The father is the middle gate of Paradise, so if you wish, guard the gate or waste it."""
"1077","1075 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', who said: I heard Dhakwan Abu Salih say: When a guest alighted with Abu al-Darda, he would say: Are you staying so we entertain you, or departing so we provide you? If he said: Departing, he would say: I shall inform you of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed of. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the people of wealth have taken this world and the Hereafter; they pray as we pray, strive as we strive, remember as we remember, and give charity while we have nothing to give! He said to me: ""Shall I not inform you of something which, if you do it, none who comes after will catch you, and you will catch those who preceded you? You declare Allah's greatness after every prayer thirty-four times, glorify Him thirty-three times, and praise Him thirty-three times; if you do that, you will catch those who preceded you, and none who comes after you will catch you except one who says the like of what you said."""
"1078","1076 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that two men disputed before Abu al-Darda over a handspan of land, so Abu al-Darda said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""If you are in a land and hear two men disputing over a handspan of land, leave it."" So Abu al-Darda left and went to Syria."
"1079","1077 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abu Halbas, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Allah, Almighty and Majestic, has finished for His creation five things: his lifespan, his deed, his trace, his resting place, and his provision."""
"1080","1078 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ma'dan ibn Abi Talhah, from Thawban, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever follows it until its completion is decreed has two qirats."""
"1081","1079 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, who said: It was said to Thawban, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Narrate to us. He said: You have lied against me and said of me what I did not say. They said: Narrate to us. So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There is no servant who prostrates to Allah a prostration but Allah, Almighty and Majestic, raises him a degree by it or removes a sin from him by it."""
"1082","1080 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, who said: He mentioned Abu Asma al-Rahabi and mentioned Thawban, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best dinars are a dinar a man spends upon his dependents, a dinar he spends upon his mount in the path of Allah, and a dinar he spends upon his companions in the path of Allah."""
"1083","1081 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The visitor of the sick is in the harvest of Paradise until he returns."""
"1084","1082 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us that Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to him that Abu Qilabah narrated to him that Abu Asma narrated to him that Thawban narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."""
"1085","1083 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, who said: The daughter of Hubayrah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a large gold ring on her hand — large rings — and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began striking her hand. She went to Fatimah complaining to her. Thawban said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Fatimah with me with him, and she had taken a gold necklace from her neck, and said: This was gifted to me by Abu Hasan — with the necklace in her hand. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Fatimah, would it please you that people say: Fatimah bint Muhammad with a chain of fire in her hand?"" He left and did not sit. Fatimah went to the necklace and sold it, bought a slave with its price and freed him. It reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""Praise be to Allah who saved Fatimah through me from the Fire."""
"1086","1084 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not come until tribes of my ummah join the polytheists and worship idols, and when the sword is placed upon my ummah it will not be lifted from them until the Day of Resurrection."""
"1087","1085 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from Umar ibn Ubayd al-Tamimi al-Abshami, from Thawban, freedman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""The nations are about to summon one another against you as people summon one another to their dish."" He said: It was said: Due to fewness? He said: ""No, but you will be scum like the scum of the flood; weakness will be placed in your hearts, and fear of you will be removed from the hearts of your enemies, due to your love of this world and your hatred of death."" Yunus said: This hadith was also narrated from Ibn Fadalah, from Marzuq Abu Abdullah, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1088","1086 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Judi, from Abu Balj, from Abu Shaybah al-Mahri, from Thawban, who said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vomit and break the fast."" [FLAG: print apparatus note naming Dar Hijr edition and a correction of a narrator name stripped from translation]"
"1089","1087 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Qays narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah, from Thawban, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who will guarantee for me one thing, that I accept — or I guarantee — Paradise for him?"" Thawban said: I said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""Do not ask anyone for anything."" He said: Thawban would sometimes drop his whip and dismount to pick it up himself."
"1090","1088 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Utbah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Muhajir, from Abbas ibn Salim al-Lakhmi, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz sent to Abu Sallam al-Habashi — carried by post until he came to him — and said: I sent to you to hear directly from you the hadith of Thawban concerning the Hawd. Abu Sallam said: I heard Thawban say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""My Hawd extends from Adan Abyan to Amman al-Balqa; its cups are like the number of the stars of the sky; its water is sweeter than honey — or he said: whiter than milk — whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst thereafter. The first to come to me at it are the poor of my ummah."" Umar stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they? He said: ""They are the disheveled of hair, the dusty of clothes, who do not marry the pampered women and for whom the doors of the courts are not opened."" He said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: By Allah, I have married the pampered women — Fatimah bint Abd al-Malik — and the doors of the courts have been opened for me; unless Allah shows me mercy, indeed by Allah I shall not oil my head until it is disheveled, nor wash the garment next to my skin until it is dirty."
"1091","1089 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Be upright, though you will never encompass; know that the best of your religion is prayer, and none preserves ablution but a believer."" This hadith is also narrated from al-Walid ibn Muslim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Abu Kabshah, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1092","1090 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Ubayd al-Kala'i, from Zuhayr ibn Salim or Ibn Yasar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""For every forgetfulness are two prostrations after the salutation."" This hadith is also narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Thawban."
"1093","1091 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we halted for rest, each of us spreading the foreleg of his mount. Then I awoke partway through the night and there was no one before the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I set out and there were Mu'adh ibn Jabal and Abdullah ibn Qays standing. I said to them: Have you seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: No, while I heard a sound like the rumbling of a millstone. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said: ""A comer from my Lord, Almighty and Majestic, came to me and gave me the choice between admitting half my ummah into Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession."" We said: We adjure you by Allah and companionship to make us among the people of your intercession! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You are among the people of my intercession."" Men began to come saying: O Messenger of Allah, make me among the people of your intercession! And he would say: ""You are among the people of my intercession."" When they crowded upon him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, I call You to witness that my intercession is for whoever of my ummah dies without associating anything with Allah."""
"1094","1092 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray over the funeral of a man of the Ansar, and I heard him say: ""O Allah, bless him, forgive him, have mercy on him, grant him health and pardon him, wash him with water, snow, and hail, cleanse him of sins and errors as the white garment is cleansed of filth, replace his abode with an abode better than his abode and a family better than his family, and protect him from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the Fire."" Awf said: I saw myself in that place wishing I were in the place of the Ansari because of what I heard of the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him. This hadith is also narrated from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf. And I saw this hadith in another place from Abu Dawud, from al-Faraj ibn Fadalah, who said: Ismah ibn Rashid narrated to me, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Awf."
"1095","1093 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ayyub al-Ghafiqi, from his uncle Iyas ibn Amir, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: When {So glorify the Name of your Lord, the Magnificent} was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Place it in your bowing."" When {Glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High} was revealed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Place it in your prostrations."""
"1096","1094 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ulayy, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: ""Three hours the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid us to pray in them or to bury our dead in them: when the sun rises shining until it ascends, when the noon-standing stands until the sun declines, and when it inclines toward setting until it sets."""
"1097","1095 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ba'jah al-Juhani, who said: Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the sacrificial animals among his Companions, and a young goat fell to me, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sacrifice it."""
"1098","1096 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jarir al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Bayan and Isma'il, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Verses have been sent down upon me, none greater than which has been seen"" — meaning the two Mu'awwidhat."
"1099","1097 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from a man, from Abu Ali, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that they were on a journey, and they wanted him to lead them in prayer but he refused and said: Let a man among you step forward, until I tell you why I do not lead you! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever leads a people and completes the prayer with them has reward for him and for them; if he does not do so, they have completion and he has deficiency."""
"1100","1098 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Nashit, from Ka'b ibn Alqamah, from Abu al-Haytham, who said: It was said to Uqbah ibn Amir: We have neighbors who drink wine and do such-and-such. He said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever sees a fault and conceals it is like one who revives a buried infant girl from her grave."""
"1101","1099 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Sallam, from Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Azraq, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Allah, Almighty and Majestic, admits three by a single arrow into Paradise: its maker who seeks good by his craft, the one who shoots it, and the one who supplies it."""
"1102","1100 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sallam, from Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Azraq, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Shoot and ride, and that you shoot is more beloved to me than that you ride. Everything with which a man amuses himself is false except a man's shooting with his bow, disciplining his horse, or playing with his wife, for these are of the truth. Whoever abandons shooting after learning it has disbelieved in what he learned."""
"1103","1101 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: I performed ablution and entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was addressing, and I heard him say: ""Whoever performs ablution well, then prays the prescribed prayer, guarding it and comprehending it until he completes it, is as the day his mother bore him."""
"1104","1102 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Qays al-Judhami, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever frees a slave, his ransom from the Fire is limb for limb."""
"1105","1103 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from one who heard Uqbah ibn Amir say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and recited {And prepare against them whatever you are able of power}, and said: ""Verily, power is shooting; verily, power is shooting."""
"1106","1104 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Yazid Abu Shuja', from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Hanash, from Fadalah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a necklace in which was a bead attached with gold, and a man bought it for seven — or nine — dinars, and mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""No, until it is distinguished from it."""
"1107","1105 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I was given the Seven in place of the Torah, the hundreds in place of the Psalms, the oft-repeated in place of the Gospel, and I was favored with the Mufassal."""
"1108","1106 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, he said: Abu Sa'd al-Shami narrated to me, who said: I saw Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' — who had companionship — praying in the mosque of Damascus wearing sandals; he spat beneath his left foot then rubbed it on the ground. When he had prayed, I said: Do you do this while you are among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! He said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"1109","1107 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, that Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani said: O Messenger of Allah, I am in a land whose people are People of the Book who eat pork and drink wine, so what of their vessels and pots? He said: ""Leave them so long as you find any alternative to them; when you find no alternative to them, rinse them with water"" — or he said: ""wash them"" — ""then cook in them and eat."" He said: And I think he said: ""And drink."""
"1110","1108 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, that Abu Tha'labah said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I send my dog and it catches game? He said: ""When you send your trained dog and mention the name of Allah and it catches, eat; and when you send your untrained dog and it catches, if you reach its slaughter then eat, and if you do not reach its slaughter then do not eat."""
"1111","1109 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Tha'labah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every fanged beast of prey and the eating of domestic donkeys"" — or he said: ""tame ones."" And Hushaym narrates part of this hadith from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, from Abu Tha'labah."
"1112","1110 - Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard Alqamah ibn Wa'il al-Hadrami narrating from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him land as a fief — I know it only as: in Hadramawt."
"1113","1111 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard Alqamah ibn Wa'il al-Hadrami narrating that Suwayd ibn Tariq asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have grapes which we press — and he mentioned wine — and he forbade him. He said: It is a medicine! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Rather, it is a disease."" Abu Bishr said: In this book of mine there is no ""from his father."" And Abu Mas'ud said: ""from his father."""
"1114","1112 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Alqamah ibn Wa'il, that Salamah ibn Yazid stood up to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was addressing after Asr and said: What if there are rulers over us after you who ask us for what is due to them and withhold from us? He fell silent, then he repeated the question as if he grew angry, and fell silent, so al-Ash'ath pulled him and said: By Allah, I shall keep asking him until the sun sets or he answers me! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Upon them is what they were charged with, and upon you is what you were charged with; listen to them and obey."" Wahb narrated this hadith from Shu'bah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Alqamah, from his father, that Salamah ibn Yazid."
"1115","1113 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, from his father, from Wa'il al-Hadrami, who said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I shall memorize his prayer! He opened the prayer, declared takbir, and raised his hands until they reached his ears, and took his left with his right. When he intended to bow, he declared takbir and raised his hands as he had raised them when he opened the prayer, and placed his palms upon his knees when he bowed. When he raised his head from bowing, he raised his hands as he had raised them when he opened the prayer. Then he prostrated and spread his left foot and sat upon it. He said: Then he placed his right palm upon his right thigh and his left hand upon his left thigh, and began supplicating thus — meaning with the forefinger, pointing with it."
"1116","1114 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he said: I heard Abu al-Bakhtari narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Yahsabi, from Wa'il al-Hadrami, that he prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he would declare takbir when lowering and when rising, raise his hands at the takbir, and give salutations to his right and to his left. Shu'bah said: Aban ibn Taghlib said to me: In this hadith is ""until the whiteness of his face appears."" So I mentioned that to Amr: Is it in the hadith ""until the whiteness of his face appears""? Amr said: Something like that."
"1117","1115 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, who said: One of my household narrated to me, from my father, that he prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave salutations to his right and to his left."
"1118","1116 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il al-Ta'i, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, and a man entered and said: Allah is Most Great, greatly; praise be to Allah abundantly; glory be to Allah and with His praise morning and evening. When he had prayed, he said: ""Who said the words?"" The man said: I, O Messenger of Allah, and I intended nothing by them but good. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I saw the doors of heaven opened, never stopping short of the Throne."""
"1119","1117 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Kuhayl informed me, he said: I heard Hujr Abu al-Anbas, who said: I heard Alqamah ibn Wa'il narrating from Wa'il — and I had heard it from Wa'il — that he prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he recited {Not of those who earned anger, nor of those astray}, he said: ""Amin,"" lowering his voice with it, placed his right hand upon his left hand, and gave salutations to his right and to his left."
"1120","1118 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Alqamah ibn Wa'il, from his father, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when two disputants came disputing over land: one of them Imru' al-Qays ibn Abis al-Kindi and the other Rabi'ah ibn Aydan. Imru' al-Qays said: O Messenger of Allah, this one has seized my land! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Your proof."" He said: I have no proof! He said: ""Then he swears."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, then he will take it! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You have nothing but that."" When he stood to swear, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If he swears wrongfully to take his land, he shall meet Allah while He is angry with him."""
"1121","1119 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Adi ibn Hatim, who said: A man bore witness before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has gone aright, and whoever disobeys them both has erred. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Be silent; an evil preacher are you."""
"1122","1120 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Tamim al-Ta'i, from Adi ibn Hatim, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath and sees something else better than it, let him do what is better and abandon it."""
"1123","1121 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, that a man asked Adi ibn Hatim for two hundred dirhams, and he grew angry at its smallness and swore not to give him. Then he said: Had I not heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever swears an oath and sees something else better than it, let him do what is better and expiate his oath,"" I would not have given you anything; but it is yours in my grant."
"1124","1122 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he heard Abdullah ibn Amr, freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, narrating that Adi ibn Hatim was asked and swore not to give, then gave. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever swears an oath and sees something else better than it, let him do what is better and expiate his oath."""
"1125","1123 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Sha'bi, from Adi, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the mi'rad and he said: ""If it strikes with its edge and kills, eat; if it strikes with its side and kills, it is beaten to death, so do not eat."" I said: I send my dog. He said: ""When you send your dog upon game and mention Allah's name and it catches, eat; if it eats of it, do not eat, for it only caught for itself."" I said: I send my dog and find with my dog a dog that caught, and I do not know which of them caught it! He said: ""Then do not eat; you mentioned Allah's name only over your dog and did not mention it over the other."""
"1126","1124 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from al-Sha'bi, from Adi, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I send my dog upon game — and he mentioned the like of it."
"1127","1125 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Warqa narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Adi ibn Hatim, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game with the mi'rad. He said: ""When you shoot game with the mi'rad and it pierces, eat; if it does not pierce, do not eat"" — or he said: ""If it strikes with its side, do not eat."" Abu Dawud was in doubt."
"1128","1126 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Warqa narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Adi ibn Hatim, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we have trained dogs which we send upon game and they hold for us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If they are trained and hold for you and kill, eat, so long as no other dog joins them."""
"1129","1127 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, who said: I heard Murayy ibn Qatari say: I heard Adi ibn Hatim narrating that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I take game but find nothing to slaughter it with except flint and a stick! He said: ""Shed the blood with whatever you wish and mention the name of Allah."""
"1130","1128 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard Murayy ibn Qatari narrating from Adi ibn Hatim, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father used to uphold kinship. He said: And he mentioned noble traits of character, then said: ""Your father intended a matter and attained it."""
"1131","1129 - And from Adi, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, food which I do not abandon except from scrupulousness. He said: ""Then do not abandon food in which you resemble Christianity."""
"1132","1130 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he heard Khaythamah, he heard Adi ibn Hatim, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Fire and sought refuge from it and turned his face away, then mentioned the Fire and sought refuge from it and turned his face away, then mentioned the Fire and sought refuge from it and turned his face away. Then he said: ""Fear the Fire even with half a date; if you find none, then with a good word."""
"1133","1131 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq say: Give charity, for I heard Abdullah ibn Ma'qil say: I heard Adi ibn Hatim say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Fear the Fire even with half a date; if you find none, then with a good word."""
"1134","1132 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from more than one who narrated to him from Adi ibn Hatim, that he narrated to them, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when highway robbery was mentioned, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Only a little time shall come upon you until a lone woman traveler journeys between Makkah and Madinah with none taking her halter; by Allah, only a little shall come upon you until a man takes a handful of gold and finds none among you to accept it from him. And there is none among you but shall meet Allah, Almighty and Majestic, with no interpreter between him and Him; he will look right and left and see nothing but the Fire. Whoever among you is able to shield his face from the Fire even with half a date, let him do so."""
"1135","1133 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, who said: ""There is none among you but shall meet Allah, Almighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection with no interpreter between him and Him; he will look to his right and to his left and see nothing but what he sent forth, then he will look and there is the Fire; let each of you fear the Fire even with half a date."" Abu Dawud did not raise it, while the companions of al-A'mash raised this hadith: al-Thawri and Abu Usamah, and I think Abu Mu'awiyah also."
"1136","1134 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhill ibn Khalifah, who said: I heard Adi ibn Hatim say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Fear the Fire even with half a date; if you find none, then with a good word."""
"1137","1135 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from one who heard Adi ibn Hatim say: When I arrived in Madinah — and it had reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I hope that Allah will place his hand in my hand"" — he said: He took me to his lodging, and a slave girl laid a cushion for us — or he said: a mat — and we sat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do you deny that it is said: There is no god but Allah? Is there any god besides Allah?"" He said: I said: No. He said: ""Do you deny that it is said: Allah is Most Great? Is there anything greater than Allah?"" He said: I said: No. He said: ""The Jews are those who earned anger, and the Christians are astray."" He said: I said: I am a Muslim. He said: I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brighten for that, or shine for that."
"1138","1136 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Adi ibn Hatim, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and find it the next day with my arrow in it! He said: ""When you find your arrow in it and know that it killed it, and see in it no trace of a beast of prey, eat."""
"1139","1137 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, who said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating from Adi ibn Hatim that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and he mentioned the like of it."
"1140","1138 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): a short spear was placed for him and he prayed toward it, with the donkey and the woman passing beyond it."
"1141","1139 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, who said: I bought a slave boy who was a cupper, and my father took his cupping instruments and broke them. I said to him: Do you break them? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of blood, the price of the dog, the earnings of the prostitute, and the stud fee of the stallion."
"1142","1140 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, who said: I heard Abu Juhayfah, who said: ""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out at midday — at midday, at midday — to al-Batha, performed ablution, and prayed Zuhr two rak'ahs and Asr two rak'ahs, with a short spear before him."" He said: Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah added in it from his father: ""The woman and the donkey would pass beyond it."""
"1143","1141 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Awn, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the image-maker."
"1144","1142 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfah, who said: ""I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw this of him white"" — pointing to the tuft below the lower lip. He said: It was said to him: Whose like were you on that day, O Abu Juhayfah? He said: I used to sharpen arrows and feather them."
"1145","1143 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I do not eat reclining."""
"1146","1144 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sharik al-Amiri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Adi al-Kindi, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The most thankful of people to Allah are the most thankful of them to people."""
"1147","1145 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Aqil ibn Talhah al-Sulami, from Muslim ibn Haysam, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we claim that we are of you or that you are of us — Abu Bishr was in doubt — so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""We are the sons of al-Nadr ibn Kinanah; we do not disown our father nor slander our mother."" He said: al-Ash'ath said: I find no one — or: no one is brought to me — who denies Quraysh descent from Kinanah but I flog him the hadd."
"1148","1146 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abdullah, who said: Whoever swears a false oath to cut off his brother's wealth with it shall meet Allah while He is angry with him. Al-Ash'ath ibn Qays came upon us and said: What did Abu Abd al-Rahman narrate to you? We informed him, and he said: He spoke the truth; concerning me this verse was revealed: {Those who purchase with Allah's covenant and their oaths a small price — they shall have no share in the Hereafter} to the end of the verse. I disputed with a man over a well before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Your proof, or his oath."" I said: Then he will swear while sinful."
"1149","1147 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Warqa narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, who said: Whoever swears a binding oath to cut off wealth with it while sinful in it shall meet Allah, Almighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him. He said: Al-Ash'ath ibn Qays al-Kindi came out to us and said: What did Abu Abd al-Rahman narrate to you? We said: Such-and-such. He said: He spoke the truth; it was revealed concerning me. I disputed with a man over a well before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Your proof, or his oath."" He said: I said: Then he will swear while sinful. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears a binding oath in which he is sinful, to cut off wealth with it, shall meet Allah, Almighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him."" And it was revealed: {Those who purchase with Allah's covenant and their oaths a small price} to the end of the verse."
"1150","1148 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed us, from Sa'id ibn Wahb, who said: I heard Khabbab say: ""We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the severity of the heat, but he did not grant our complaint."""
"1151","1149 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed us, he said: I heard Harithah ibn Mudarrib say: We entered upon Khabbab when he had been cauterized, and he said: I know no one who met of trial what I met. I remained in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finding not a dirham, while in this corner of my house there are forty thousand; had the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not forbidden us — or: forbidden — that anyone wish for death, I would have wished for it."
"1152","1150 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Abu al-Duha narrating from Masruq, from Khabbab, who said: ""I was a blacksmith in the pre-Islamic period, and I had dirhams owed by al-As ibn Wa'il, so I came to him demanding payment. He said: I shall not pay you until you disbelieve in Muhammad! I said: I shall not disbelieve in Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until Allah causes you to die then resurrects you. He said: Leave me until I die then am resurrected, and I shall have wealth and children and pay you! He said: Then this verse was revealed: {Have you seen the one who disbelieved in Our verses and said: I shall surely be given wealth and children}."""
"1153","1151 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Sari', from Amr ibn Hurayth, who said: ""I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he recited {When the sun is folded up}. When he reached this verse {And the night when it departs, and the morning when it breathes}, I said to myself: What is the night when it departs and the morning when it breathes?"""
"1154","1152 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Safar and Husayn, who both heard al-Sha'bi say: I heard Urwah ibn Abi al-Ja'd al-Bariqi say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the good? He said: ""Reward and booty."""
"1155","1153 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth narrating from Urwah ibn al-Ja'd al-Bariqi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the good? He said: ""Reward and booty."""
"1156","1154 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abu Humaydah al-Za'ini, from Urwah al-Bariqi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Horses have good tied in their forelocks."" It was said: What is the good? He said: ""Reward and spoils."""
"1157","1155 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: al-Zubayr ibn Khirrit al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind al-Ashja'i narrated to me, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was seen stroking the cheek of a horse, and he was asked about that, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Jibril blamed me concerning the horse."" Abu Bishr said: Ahmad ibn al-Furat informed us, from Muslim ibn Ibrahim, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from al-Zubayr ibn Khirrit, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, from Urwah."
"1158","1156 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla narrating from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, who said: Successive remembrances which their sayer — or he said: their doer — shall not fail in: that you declare Allah's greatness thirty-four times, glorify Him thirty-three times, and praise Him thirty-three times after every prayer. Al-Hakam said: I have not abandoned them since. And Abu Amir narrated this hadith from Sufyan, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1159","1157 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, who said: Ka'b ibn Ujrah met me and said: Shall I not gift you a gift? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, and we said: We know how to greet you, but how do we send blessings upon you? He said: ""Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed the family of Ibrahim; You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, grant favor to Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You granted favor to the family of Ibrahim; You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."""
"1160","1158 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Ma'qil say: I sat with Ka'b ibn Ujrah in this mosque and asked him about Allah's saying, Almighty and Majestic: {Then a ransom of fasting, charity, or sacrifice}. He said: It was revealed concerning me; I was carried to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with lice scattering upon my face, and he said: ""I did not think hardship had reached you as I see! Slaughter a sheep."" I said: I cannot find one. Then it was revealed: {Then a ransom of fasting} — three days, or feeding six poor persons half a sa'; it was revealed concerning me specifically, and it is for you generally."
"1161","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from a freedman of Banu Salim, from his father, from Ka'b ibn Ujra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you performs ablution and then goes out for prayer, he is in prayer, so none of you should interlock his fingers after performing ablution or after entering the prayer."
"1162","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, saying: Musa al-Hilali narrated to us, from his father, from Ka'b, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us in the mosque and said: Who is here? Do you hear? After me there will be rulers who act without obedience to Allah, so whoever shares in their deeds and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me and I am not of him, and whoever does not share in their deeds and does not help them in their wrongdoing is of me and I am of him."
"1163","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hushaym and Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujra, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the time of al-Hudaybiya while in ihram, and the polytheists had come between us and the House, and I had thick hair, and lice began falling upon me, or he said upon my face, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Do your vermin harm you? I said: Yes. He said: Then shave your head, and fast three days, or feed six poor persons, or offer a sacrifice."
"1164","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq, from his uncle, who said: I went out with Ka'b ibn Ujra on the day of Eid and he did not pray before it, and when we had prayed he saw the people going as one body toward the mosque, so he said: What are these people doing? I said: They are going to the mosque. He said: This is an innovation and an abandonment of the Sunna."
"1165","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Furat al-Qazzaz, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfa ibn Asid al-Ghifari, one of the people of al-Suffa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were discussing the Hour, and he said: The Hour will not come until there are ten signs: the smoke, the Dajjal, the Beast, the rising of the sun from its west, three eclipses, an eclipse in the east, an eclipse in the west, and an eclipse in the Arabian Peninsula, the descent of Isa son of Maryam, the opening of Gog and Magog, and a fire emerging from the depths of Aden driving the people to the gathering place."
"1166","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfa ibn Asid, that news of the death of the Negus came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Your brother has died in a land other than yours, so stand and pray over him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lined them up behind him and prayed over him."
"1167","Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Talha ibn Amr and Jarir ibn Hazim; as for Talha, he said: Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi informed me that Abu al-Tufayl narrated to him from Hudhayfa ibn Asid al-Ghifari Abu Surayha, and as for Jarir, he said: from Abdullah ibn Umayr, from a man of the family of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, and the hadith of Talha is the fuller and better of the two, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Beast and said: It will emerge three times in history; it will emerge in the farthest desert and its mention will not enter the town, meaning Makka, then it will hide for a long time, then emerge another emergence less than that, so its mention will spread among the desert people and enter the town, meaning Makka. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then while the people are in the greatest mosque in sanctity to Allah, the best and noblest of them, the Sacred Mosque, nothing will startle them except that it will be bellowing between the Corner and the Station, shaking the dust from its head, so the people will scatter from it in groups and together, and a group of believers will remain firm, knowing they cannot escape Allah, so it will begin with them and make their faces bright until they become like brilliant stars, and it will go forth in the land, no seeker catching it and no fleer escaping it, until a man will seek refuge from it in prayer, and it will come to him from behind and say: O so-and-so, now you pray! Then he will turn to it and it will mark him on his face, then go on, and people will share in wealth and accompany one another in the cities, the believer distinguished from the disbeliever, until the believer will say: O disbeliever, pay me my due! And the disbeliever will say: O believer, pay me my due!"
"1168","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Ansari saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plundering and mutilation."
"1169","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qurra ibn Khalid narrated to us, Mu'awiya ibn Qurra narrated to us, from his father, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, show me the Seal! He said: Put in your hand. So I put my hand into his collar and felt and looked at the Seal, and it was upon the cartilage of his shoulder like an egg, and that did not prevent him from supplicating for me while my hand was inside his collar."
"1170","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiya al-Ju'fi narrated to us, saying: Urwa ibn Abdullah al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from his father, who said: I reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his buttons were undone, and you would never see Mu'awiya and his son except with their buttons undone."
"1171","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harun ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Qatada narrated to us, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from his father, who said: In the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we would be driven away with insistence from standing between the pillars in prayer."
"1172","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting three days of the month is the fast of a lifetime, and its breaking."
"1173","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from his father, that an Ansari man with a son of his used to visit the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him one day: O so-and-so, do you love him? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, may Allah love you as I love him! Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him and asked about him, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, his son has died! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Would he not be pleased, or: Will you not be pleased, that you will not come to any gate of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection except that he will come hastening to open it for you? Then a man said: O Messenger of Allah, is that for him alone or for all of us? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather, for all of you."
"1174","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Mu'awiya ibn Qurra narrated to us, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Sham become corrupt there will be no good in you; a group of my community will remain victorious, those who forsake them will not harm them, until the Hour comes."
"1175","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, who said: My father came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he had milked and tied the udder."
"1176","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, that Ibn Mas'ud went to bring the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a tooth-stick, and they began looking at the thinness of his leg, or wondering at the thinness of his leg, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are heavier on the Scale than Uhud. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it, while others besides Abu Dawud said: from Shu'ba, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from his father."
"1177","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar al-Mujashi'i, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day in his sermon: Indeed my Lord commanded me to teach you what you were ignorant of from what He taught me this day: Every wealth I grant My servant is lawful, and I created My servants all upright, but the devils came to them and diverted them from their religion and forbade to them what I had made lawful for them and commanded them to associate with Me what I sent no authority for. And Allah looked at the people of the earth and abhorred them, their Arabs and non-Arabs, except remnants of the People of the Book, and said: O Muhammad, I have sent you to test you and to test others through you, and I have sent down upon you a Book that water cannot wash away, which you recite sleeping and awake. And Allah commanded me to rouse Quraysh, so I said: My Lord, then they will split my head and leave it like a loaf of bread! So He said: Expel them as they expelled you, raid them and you will be reinforced, spend and it will be spent upon you, send an army and We will send five like it, and fight with those who obey you against those who disobey you. And he said: The people of Paradise are three: a just, charitable, guided ruler, a merciful man tender-hearted toward every Muslim relative, and a chaste poor man who gives charity. And the people of Hell are five: the weak one with no restraint, those among you who are followers seeking neither family nor wealth, the treacherous one whose greed for anything, however small, is never hidden except that he betrays it, a man who never begins morning or evening except that he deceives you concerning your family and wealth, and he mentioned miserliness or lying, and the foul-mouthed obscene one. Abu Dawud said: Then Hammam narrated to us, saying: We were with Qatada and we mentioned this hadith, and Yunus al-Haddadi, and there was none among us more retentive than he, said: Qatada did not hear this hadith from Mutarrif. So we criticized him for that, and he said: Ask him! But we were awed of him, then a Bedouin came, so we said to the Bedouin: Ask Qatada about the sermon of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning the hadith of Iyad ibn Himar, did you hear it from Mutarrif? So the Bedouin said: O Abu al-Khattab, tell me about the sermon of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning the hadith of Iyad, did you hear it from Mutarrif? So he became angry and said: Three narrated it to me from him; Yazid, the brother, son of Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, narrated it to me, and al-Ala ibn Ziyad al-Adawi narrated it to me from him, and he mentioned a third whom Hammam did not retain."
"1178","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Imran al-Qattan and Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada; Hammam said: from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, while Imran said: from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man of my people inferior to me insults me? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two persons trading insults are two devils accusing and belying each other, so whatever they say is upon the one who began, until the wronged one transgresses."
"1179","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: I heard Khalid al-Hadhdha narrating from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar al-Mujashi'i, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever picks up a lost item should call just witnesses, or a just witness, and should neither conceal nor hide it; if its owner comes he is most entitled to it, otherwise it is the wealth of Allah which He gives to whom He wills. Abu Bishr said: And I saw in another place, from Abu Dawud, from Shu'ba, from Khalid, from Yazid, from Iyad, without Mutarrif therein."
"1180","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Himar, who said: I gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a gift, or he said a she-camel, and he said to me: Have you become Muslim? I said: No. So he refused to accept it, and said: We do not accept the gifts of the polytheists. I said to al-Hasan: What is the gift of the polytheists? He said: Their support."
"1181","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Imran narrated to us, from Qatada, from Yazid ibn Abdullah, from Iyad ibn Himar, who said: I gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a she-camel, or he said a gift, and he said: Have you become Muslim? I said: No. He said: I have been forbidden the gifts of the polytheists."
"1182","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Dabbi narrated to us, from al-Mughira, from his father, from Shu'ba ibn al-Taw'am, from Qays ibn Asim, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about confederacy in Islam, and he said: There is no confederacy in Islam, but uphold the confederacy of the pre-Islamic age."
"1183","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, who said: I heard Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrating from Hakim ibn Qays al-Tamimi that his father enjoined his sons at his death, saying: When I die do not wail over me, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not wailed over."
"1184","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard Qabisa ibn Hulb narrating from his father that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, and he mentioned charity, saying: None of you should come with a sheep that is bleating."
"1185","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Simak, from Qabisa ibn Hulb, from his father, that he prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would depart turning to both his sides."
"1186","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, who said: I heard Waki' ibn Udus narrating from his uncle Abu Razin al-Uqayli that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the believer is one part of forty parts of prophethood, and it is suspended on the foot of a bird as long as it is not spoken of, but when it is spoken of it falls. He said: And I think he said: And do not speak of it except to a beloved one or an intelligent one."
"1187","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Ya'la ibn Ata informed me, saying: I heard Waki' ibn Udus narrating from Abu Razin al-Uqayli, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how does Allah give life to the dead? He said: Have you not passed by a barren valley and then passed by it green? He said: Yes. He said: So likewise is the resurrection, or he said: Thus Allah gives life to the dead."
"1188","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, who said: I heard Waki' ibn Udus narrating from Abu Razin al-Uqayli, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother used to uphold kinship and do such and such, but she died a polytheist! So where is she? He said: She is in the Fire. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, then where is your mother? He said: Would you not be pleased that your mother be with my mother."
"1189","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: al-Nu'man ibn Salim informed me, from Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, from Abu Razin al-Uqayli, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is a very old man unable to perform Hajj or Umra or to travel! He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father, or Umra."
"1190","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from Waki' ibn Hudus, from Abu Razin, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our Lord laughs at the despair of His servants and the nearness of His relief. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, does the Lord laugh, blessed and exalted is He?! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. Then he said: We shall never lack good from a Lord who laughs."
"1191","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from Waki' ibn Hudus, from Abu Razin, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked being questioned, but when Abu Razin asked him it pleased him. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, where was our Lord before He created the heavens and the earth? He said: He was in mist, above which was no air and below which was no air, then He created the Throne upon the water."
"1192","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from Waki' ibn Hudus, from Abu Razin, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, will all of us see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Yes. I said: And what is the sign of that in His creation? He said: Do not all of you see the moon alone by itself? I said: Yes. He said: Then Allah is greater."
"1193","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Utba narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no two witrs in one night."
"1194","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Utba narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us is in prayer and touches his private part, should he repeat ablution? He said: No, it is only a part of you."
"1195","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Utba narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman to withhold herself from her husband, even if upon a camel saddle."
"1196","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Utba narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Does a man pray in a single garment? He remained silent until the prayer came, then he prayed in a single garment crossing its two ends."
"1197","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Habib ibn Zayd al-Ansari narrated to me, saying: I heard Abbad ibn Tamim narrating from Abdullah ibn Zayd, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and rub his forearms."
"1198","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to pray for rain, turning his back to the people and facing the qibla, turning his cloak inside out, and prayed two rak'ahs with the people reciting aloud."
"1199","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reclining in the mosque placing one foot upon the other."
"1200","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Kharija ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya al-Ansari, from his father, who said: Abdullah ibn Zayd said to us: Shall I not perform for you the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? We said: Yes. So he rinsed his mouth and nose with a single handful three times, then washed his face three times, then washed his forearms twice each, then wiped his head moving his hands forward and back, and washed his feet three times each, then said: Such was the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
